1
00:00:20,727 --> 00:00:22,456
(Would you like to go on a business trip...)

2
00:00:22,457 --> 00:00:24,267
(with the secretaries?)

3
00:00:25,427 --> 00:00:28,597
(Busan, the city by the sea)

4
00:00:30,637 --> 00:00:33,807
(Busan International Film Festival)

5
00:00:34,107 --> 00:00:35,206
(Celebrating its 31st anniversary,)

6
00:00:35,207 --> 00:00:36,937
(it's grown beyond Korea's biggest film festival.)

7
00:00:37,677 --> 00:00:41,146
("Busan International Film Festival Joins the A-List...")

8
00:00:41,147 --> 00:00:43,577
("Alongside Cannes and Berlin")

9
00:00:44,917 --> 00:00:47,787
(Globally recognized prestige, unprecedented scale)

10
00:00:48,017 --> 00:00:51,827
(This dazzling festival brings together...)

11
00:00:52,087 --> 00:00:54,626
(some of the biggest names in world cinema.)

12
00:00:54,627 --> 00:00:56,957
(And the star shining brightest is today's My Star,)

13
00:00:59,397 --> 00:01:04,067
(Son Suk Ku.)

14
00:01:05,567 --> 00:01:08,977
(He's the busiest actor here, having walked the red carpet twice.)

15
00:01:09,737 --> 00:01:12,506
(Today's My Star, overflowing with charm, is...)

16
00:01:12,507 --> 00:01:14,516
Suk Ku shot to stardom...

17
00:01:14,517 --> 00:01:16,016
a few years ago.

18
00:01:16,017 --> 00:01:17,847
He took Korea by storm.

19
00:01:18,317 --> 00:01:21,486
The fact that he became so popular...

20
00:01:21,487 --> 00:01:23,917
shows how uniquely charming he is.

21
00:01:26,027 --> 00:01:28,057
(You've been kidnapped by my charms.)

22
00:01:28,697 --> 00:01:31,627
("Kidnapping" a staggering 12.69 million people into theaters)

23
00:01:33,367 --> 00:01:36,337
(He played an unconventional killer...)

24
00:01:36,767 --> 00:01:39,037
(and pushed the boundaries of Korean action movies.)

25
00:01:39,867 --> 00:01:44,177
(He played an English-speaking international police officer...)

26
00:01:44,477 --> 00:01:48,417
(and took down casino criminals.)

27
00:01:48,677 --> 00:01:51,086
(In "D.P...")

28
00:01:51,087 --> 00:01:52,546
(and "A Killer Paradox,")

29
00:01:52,547 --> 00:01:54,487
(he delivered back-to-back action masterclasses.)

30
00:01:56,017 --> 00:02:01,227
(Exhausted by all that action, he started drinking soju every night.)

31
00:02:01,827 --> 00:02:06,567
(And he suddenly ventured into romance.)

32
00:02:06,827 --> 00:02:09,897
(As he was winning hearts and worshipped,)

33
00:02:10,467 --> 00:02:14,207
(he requested a meeting with the staff the day before filming.)

34
00:02:14,677 --> 00:02:16,276
(After the red carpet event,)

35
00:02:16,277 --> 00:02:19,377
(he held a top-secret meeting with the staff of My Genie Secretary.)

36
00:02:19,577 --> 00:02:21,916
This is the biggest challenge...

37
00:02:21,917 --> 00:02:22,976
of my acting career in a way.

38
00:02:22,977 --> 00:02:24,247
(The biggest challenge of his acting career?)

39
00:02:24,287 --> 00:02:25,416
So...

40
00:02:25,417 --> 00:02:26,716
he followed me,

41
00:02:26,717 --> 00:02:28,286
so I sent him a DM.

42
00:02:28,287 --> 00:02:29,917
(He got in touch with someone for the biggest challenge in his life?)

43
00:02:30,217 --> 00:02:31,386
(Who received a message that could get him into trouble?)

44
00:02:31,387 --> 00:02:32,686
Will I get in trouble?

45
00:02:32,687 --> 00:02:34,397
- I...
- I think he's a bit sensitive.

46
00:02:35,397 --> 00:02:38,697
(The next morning, at P Hotel, the heart of BIFF)

47
00:02:38,897 --> 00:02:39,966
(The one who received his message...)

48
00:02:39,967 --> 00:02:42,897
(will appear in a few seconds.)

49
00:02:43,737 --> 00:02:44,866
(Kwang Kyu arrived the day before and stayed at the hotel.)

50
00:02:44,867 --> 00:02:46,067
- Hello.
- Hello.

51
00:02:47,477 --> 00:02:49,007
Star Son.

52
00:02:49,507 --> 00:02:51,607
I followed him on Instagram,

53
00:02:52,107 --> 00:02:55,077
- and he sent me a message.
- He did?

54
00:02:55,177 --> 00:02:58,117
"Leave the hard stuff to Seo Jin."

55
00:02:59,347 --> 00:03:01,487
(My Star contacted him first.)

56
00:03:02,287 --> 00:03:03,916
(Make Seo Jin do the dirty work.)

57
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:06,927
How do you know that I follow him?

58
00:03:07,187 --> 00:03:09,026
I think he told me...

59
00:03:09,027 --> 00:03:10,556
to make Seo Jin...

60
00:03:10,557 --> 00:03:12,367
do the dirty work or something like that.

61
00:03:13,367 --> 00:03:15,266
That's when my producer instincts...

62
00:03:15,267 --> 00:03:17,167
- kicked in.
- Okay.

63
00:03:17,267 --> 00:03:18,667
(Kwang Kyu's request awakened his producer instincts.)

64
00:03:19,237 --> 00:03:21,107
"You're a good driver."

65
00:03:21,907 --> 00:03:23,707
"Can you drive for me?"

66
00:03:24,377 --> 00:03:25,676
Should I be specific about the temperature of the water?

67
00:03:25,677 --> 00:03:27,307
I could ask him to keep the water...

68
00:03:27,617 --> 00:03:29,617
at exactly 32°C.

69
00:03:30,617 --> 00:03:33,516
(After brainstorming for a while)

70
00:03:33,517 --> 00:03:34,916
At some point, I'm going to start making...

71
00:03:34,917 --> 00:03:36,456
unreasonable demands.

72
00:03:36,457 --> 00:03:38,527
(Just imagining it gets me so excited.)

73
00:03:38,657 --> 00:03:41,227
(Making Seo Jin fan him)

74
00:03:41,527 --> 00:03:43,697
(Making Seo Jin drive)

75
00:03:44,297 --> 00:03:46,167
(Grabbing Seo Jin by the collar)

76
00:03:46,667 --> 00:03:48,666
(Is today Kwang Kyu's lucky day?)

77
00:03:48,667 --> 00:03:50,967
(Kwang Kyu, just trust me.)

78
00:03:58,407 --> 00:04:00,307
Why is he making me wait for so long?

79
00:04:00,747 --> 00:04:02,116
I'm a star too.

80
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:03,217
He's here.

81
00:04:03,747 --> 00:04:04,917
Oh, you're here.

82
00:04:05,547 --> 00:04:07,657
(He showed up just as he was talking about him.)

83
00:04:08,057 --> 00:04:09,756
(Good morning.)

84
00:04:09,757 --> 00:04:10,926
I was like...

85
00:04:10,927 --> 00:04:12,687
Seo Jin, that's a nice jacket.

86
00:04:13,557 --> 00:04:15,497
It goes well with the necklace.

87
00:04:16,157 --> 00:04:17,827
- Why? It looks great.
- You look good.

88
00:04:18,927 --> 00:04:21,067
(My friend looks good.)

89
00:04:21,997 --> 00:04:23,336
The jacket looks expensive.

90
00:04:23,337 --> 00:04:24,337
(Flashing a satisfied smile)

91
00:04:24,467 --> 00:04:26,066
It's cold, isn't it?

92
00:04:26,067 --> 00:04:27,837
(I should've put on a puffer jacket too.)

93
00:04:28,777 --> 00:04:31,906
(He braced himself for Busan's winds in a cute, cozy puffer jacket.)

94
00:04:31,907 --> 00:04:33,006
Have you met Suk Ku?

95
00:04:33,007 --> 00:04:34,276
No, I haven't.

96
00:04:34,277 --> 00:04:36,317
(They head straight to where My Star is.)

97
00:04:36,617 --> 00:04:39,116
He's already in the middle of a photoshoot.

98
00:04:39,117 --> 00:04:40,447
He's in the middle of a photoshoot.

99
00:04:42,057 --> 00:04:44,327
(He's doing a photoshoot in the morning.)

100
00:04:44,787 --> 00:04:47,997
(His playful side disappears, and he radiates charisma.)

101
00:04:48,457 --> 00:04:49,926
(Time: 9am, Location: Hotel,)

102
00:04:49,927 --> 00:04:51,697
(Details: "The Blue Road" photoshoot)

103
00:04:52,527 --> 00:04:55,667
(His co-star is...)

104
00:04:56,337 --> 00:04:58,707
(one of Japan's most beloved actors, Eita Nagayama.)

105
00:05:00,167 --> 00:05:02,407
(Looking intently)

106
00:05:03,377 --> 00:05:05,507
(Hi, Suk Ku.)

107
00:05:06,807 --> 00:05:08,546
(Bowing)

108
00:05:08,547 --> 00:05:10,647
(A big smile)

109
00:05:11,317 --> 00:05:14,317
(He's already excited and happy to see them.)

110
00:05:15,257 --> 00:05:16,517
Hello.

111
00:05:16,617 --> 00:05:18,987
I'm Lee Dong Gyu. I'm Suk Ku's manager.

112
00:05:20,087 --> 00:05:22,027
(Lee Dong Gyu, Son Suk Ku's manager)

113
00:05:22,297 --> 00:05:23,497
- Hello.
- Which...

114
00:05:23,697 --> 00:05:24,697
Which agency is Suk Ku signed with?

115
00:05:24,698 --> 00:05:26,697
Stannum.

116
00:05:26,767 --> 00:05:28,296
Suk Ku started his own production company...

117
00:05:28,297 --> 00:05:30,097
and management agency.

118
00:05:30,337 --> 00:05:31,906
He's the agency's only talent.

119
00:05:31,907 --> 00:05:33,136
- Is that so?
- Yes.

120
00:05:33,137 --> 00:05:35,607
(He's also passionate about film production.)

121
00:05:36,007 --> 00:05:37,306
This is today's schedule.

122
00:05:37,307 --> 00:05:38,947
Here's the company card.

123
00:05:39,007 --> 00:05:41,247
Let me explain a little.

124
00:05:41,547 --> 00:05:43,816
Today at BIFF, his drama series "The Blue Road..."

125
00:05:43,817 --> 00:05:45,046
will be unveiled for the first time...

126
00:05:45,047 --> 00:05:46,916
at a special screening.

127
00:05:46,917 --> 00:05:48,356
Is it not a movie?

128
00:05:48,357 --> 00:05:50,587
- It's a drama.
- Is that so?

129
00:05:51,627 --> 00:05:54,257
(A new crime thriller from director Han Jun Hee)

130
00:05:54,657 --> 00:05:57,127
(Son Suk Ku, Seoul Metropolitan Police detective)

131
00:05:57,157 --> 00:06:00,297
(Eita, Tokyo Metropolitan Police detective)

132
00:06:00,427 --> 00:06:03,837
(They investigate bizarre murders that span national borders.)

133
00:06:04,097 --> 00:06:08,107
(Crime-solving buddy series following "D.P.")

134
00:06:10,537 --> 00:06:12,907
("The Blue Road")

135
00:06:13,477 --> 00:06:15,077
What's this? "Bedford Park?"

136
00:06:15,177 --> 00:06:16,576
That's the movie...

137
00:06:16,577 --> 00:06:18,986
we filmed in the US.

138
00:06:18,987 --> 00:06:20,116
- Is that a different one?
- This one...

139
00:06:20,117 --> 00:06:21,416
Yes.

140
00:06:21,417 --> 00:06:24,086
This is the outdoor stage greeting squeezed in between the two.

141
00:06:24,087 --> 00:06:25,827
- Is this a movie?
- Yes, it is.

142
00:06:26,457 --> 00:06:28,296
(He'll walk the red carpet once for "Bedford Park,")

143
00:06:28,297 --> 00:06:29,527
(a film he produced himself,)

144
00:06:29,727 --> 00:06:33,927
(and twice for the series "The Blue Road.")

145
00:06:34,537 --> 00:06:36,096
(Today's schedule is packed.)

146
00:06:36,097 --> 00:06:37,536
After finishing this,

147
00:06:37,537 --> 00:06:39,706
he'll stop by here for a Q and A session.

148
00:06:39,707 --> 00:06:41,406
We need to figure out...

149
00:06:41,407 --> 00:06:43,207
how he'll get from one event to the next.

150
00:06:43,307 --> 00:06:45,446
The whole schedule...

151
00:06:45,447 --> 00:06:47,346
is pretty tight.

152
00:06:47,347 --> 00:06:49,416
We don't have much time.

153
00:06:49,417 --> 00:06:51,016
- Right.
- That's a short lunch break.

154
00:06:51,017 --> 00:06:52,287
It's short.

155
00:06:53,187 --> 00:06:56,887
(While the secretaries are checking his tight schedule...)

156
00:06:57,617 --> 00:06:59,657
(Do you see them?)

157
00:07:00,287 --> 00:07:05,197
(They're my managers for today.)

158
00:07:05,427 --> 00:07:07,526
And I don't usually...

159
00:07:07,527 --> 00:07:09,567
carry a bag for him.

160
00:07:10,337 --> 00:07:12,066
They usually have tea tables and stuff,

161
00:07:12,067 --> 00:07:13,307
so I don't carry a bag.

162
00:07:13,537 --> 00:07:16,777
This is a military-style tactical vest.

163
00:07:17,337 --> 00:07:20,976
(My Star navigates rough filming locations.)

164
00:07:20,977 --> 00:07:22,876
It's an X-shaped harness.

165
00:07:22,877 --> 00:07:24,586
This is something we only use when we're shooting on location.

166
00:07:24,587 --> 00:07:25,847
But just in case you might need it...

167
00:07:25,917 --> 00:07:28,087
You can keep his phone in here.

168
00:07:28,117 --> 00:07:30,787
Whenever Suk Ku hands me his phone, I'll keep it in this vest.

169
00:07:31,527 --> 00:07:33,326
It feels like I'm going on a march.

170
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:35,756
Looks like there's a military drill today.

171
00:07:35,757 --> 00:07:37,127
- What?
- You're heading out for a drill.

172
00:07:37,557 --> 00:07:38,866
(Armed with a phone)

173
00:07:38,867 --> 00:07:39,867
Put the water in.

174
00:07:39,897 --> 00:07:41,196
(Putting in the water)

175
00:07:41,197 --> 00:07:42,736
Is this for the water?

176
00:07:42,737 --> 00:07:43,737
Is this a grenade?

177
00:07:44,267 --> 00:07:45,736
That's the original purpose.

178
00:07:45,737 --> 00:07:46,807
- Is that so?
- Yes.

179
00:07:47,137 --> 00:07:48,306
Not bad.

180
00:07:48,307 --> 00:07:50,606
(He's all geared up to assist him with action scenes.)

181
00:07:50,607 --> 00:07:52,876
Today's the day of Foal Eagle.

182
00:07:52,877 --> 00:07:54,407
(What on earth are they doing?)

183
00:07:55,117 --> 00:07:58,317
(While the secretaries are playing together)

184
00:07:59,987 --> 00:08:02,487
(Thumbs up. It's over!)

185
00:08:02,917 --> 00:08:06,257
(My Star's first schedule is over.)

186
00:08:06,957 --> 00:08:07,957
The makeup team.

187
00:08:08,427 --> 00:08:09,957
- Does he have one?
- Yes.

188
00:08:10,097 --> 00:08:11,097
Hello.

189
00:08:11,297 --> 00:08:12,696
(As soon as he finished it, he rushed over to give them a bow.)

190
00:08:12,697 --> 00:08:14,327
- Have you been doing well?
- Yes, I've been doing great.

191
00:08:14,667 --> 00:08:15,897
You look like you've lost weight.

192
00:08:16,797 --> 00:08:18,166
Have you been doing well?

193
00:08:18,167 --> 00:08:19,237
- Yes, I've been doing great.
- Good.

194
00:08:19,967 --> 00:08:22,407
(Do they know each other?)

195
00:08:22,777 --> 00:08:26,177
(He went to see "Uncle Vanya,")

196
00:08:26,307 --> 00:08:29,247
(the play Seo Jin starred in back in May,)

197
00:08:29,447 --> 00:08:32,847
(and met him backstage.)

198
00:08:33,547 --> 00:08:34,717
It's been a long time.

199
00:08:34,957 --> 00:08:36,416
Star Son.

200
00:08:36,417 --> 00:08:37,586
(He also greets Kwang Kyu, who has worked with him.)

201
00:08:37,587 --> 00:08:38,787
- Have you been doing well?
- Yes.

202
00:08:39,057 --> 00:08:40,486
- His English is great.
- What?

203
00:08:40,487 --> 00:08:41,856
- His English is excellent.
- He complimented...

204
00:08:41,857 --> 00:08:43,457
your English a lot.

205
00:08:43,627 --> 00:08:44,666
Do you speak Japanese too?

206
00:08:44,667 --> 00:08:45,927
Do you speak Japanese with the Japanese actor?

207
00:08:46,167 --> 00:08:47,526
- I did learn Japanese, - Okay.

208
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:49,696
but I just memorized some phrases like they were song lyrics.

209
00:08:49,697 --> 00:08:51,537
- Is that so?
- Yes.

210
00:08:51,637 --> 00:08:53,636
Here... Where is he?

211
00:08:53,637 --> 00:08:54,736
(He introduces Eita to the secretaries.)

212
00:08:54,737 --> 00:08:56,337
Eita, this is...

213
00:08:56,877 --> 00:08:58,407
- Hello.
- This is Eita Nagayama.

214
00:08:58,707 --> 00:09:00,477
Nice to meet you.

215
00:09:00,607 --> 00:09:04,177
This is Kim Kwang Kyu, a Korean actor.

216
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:06,447
This is Lee Seo Jin.

217
00:09:06,887 --> 00:09:08,717
- Nice to meet you.
- Oh my.

218
00:09:09,157 --> 00:09:11,526
- Oh my. His Korean is good.
- He can speak Korean.

219
00:09:11,527 --> 00:09:12,926
He worked hard to learn Korean.

220
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:14,956
He speaks Korean...

221
00:09:14,957 --> 00:09:17,057
- Does he do it better?
- better than I speak Japanese.

222
00:09:17,157 --> 00:09:18,296
So...

223
00:09:18,297 --> 00:09:22,167
I saw your show.

224
00:09:22,197 --> 00:09:25,067
It was very entertaining.

225
00:09:25,437 --> 00:09:27,266
- Yes.
- Did you watch it?

226
00:09:27,267 --> 00:09:28,707
- Did you watch it?
- Yes.

227
00:09:29,877 --> 00:09:31,947
Hello. Welcome.

228
00:09:32,077 --> 00:09:33,907
Your Japanese is good.

229
00:09:34,007 --> 00:09:35,817
- No. That's all he knows.
- Is that so?

230
00:09:36,147 --> 00:09:40,287
What does your father do?

231
00:09:40,887 --> 00:09:44,787
(Getting his first taste of the spicy side of Korean shows)

232
00:09:44,887 --> 00:09:45,927
I don't know.

233
00:09:47,627 --> 00:09:49,026
He said, "I don't know."

234
00:09:49,027 --> 00:09:50,157
(Eita, we apologize for what he said.)

235
00:09:50,627 --> 00:09:51,666
Have you eaten?

236
00:09:51,667 --> 00:09:52,927
- I had breakfast.
- You did?

237
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:54,127
What are you having for lunch?

238
00:09:54,397 --> 00:09:55,596
- Well...
- Are you on a diet?

239
00:09:55,597 --> 00:09:56,997
- No.
- So you have no problem?

240
00:09:57,337 --> 00:09:59,036
- Let me know if you want something.
- Something I want?

241
00:09:59,037 --> 00:10:00,136
- We have plenty of time.
- Okay.

242
00:10:00,137 --> 00:10:01,137
What should we do now?

243
00:10:02,677 --> 00:10:04,807
- Why are you so gentle?
- Sorry?

244
00:10:04,847 --> 00:10:06,607
We talked about this.

245
00:10:06,877 --> 00:10:07,877
- Why are you so gentle?
- Sorry?

246
00:10:07,878 --> 00:10:09,877
(Flustered)

247
00:10:13,547 --> 00:10:15,486
Give me some time. I'll think about what to do.

248
00:10:15,487 --> 00:10:16,787
Okay.

249
00:10:17,857 --> 00:10:19,426
- We have plenty of time.
- Yes.

250
00:10:19,427 --> 00:10:21,627
- So...
- I trust you.

251
00:10:22,127 --> 00:10:24,966
Do you have to go out for the greeting now?

252
00:10:24,967 --> 00:10:26,727
- Yes.
- I see.

253
00:10:26,767 --> 00:10:28,096
Are you wearing that outfit for the stage greeting?

254
00:10:28,097 --> 00:10:30,337
I think I'll get changed.

255
00:10:30,437 --> 00:10:31,966
- It won't take long.
- Sure. Go get changed.

256
00:10:31,967 --> 00:10:33,467
(My Star is getting changed.)

257
00:10:34,707 --> 00:10:36,837
(He enters the fitting room.)

258
00:10:37,007 --> 00:10:39,877
Kwang Kyu, why don't you make some coffee for Suk Ku?

259
00:10:40,107 --> 00:10:41,716
- You think I should?
- Why not?

260
00:10:41,717 --> 00:10:42,746
(The secretaries got this for My Star.)

261
00:10:42,747 --> 00:10:44,786
This is sugar-free.

262
00:10:44,787 --> 00:10:45,847
