520
00:20:41,878 --> 00:20:44,446
When 2 or 3 projects become hits back-to-back,

521
00:20:44,447 --> 00:20:47,447
- that really cements your status.
- Right.

522
00:20:48,757 --> 00:20:50,886
My life literally changed...

523
00:20:50,887 --> 00:20:52,887
overnight.

524
00:20:54,127 --> 00:20:56,526
- The world has flipped upside down.
- Yes.

525
00:20:56,527 --> 00:20:57,627
That's how I felt.

526
00:20:58,127 --> 00:20:59,627
This is a completely different story,

527
00:20:59,767 --> 00:21:01,867
but my all-time favorite drama is "Damo."

528
00:21:03,237 --> 00:21:05,307
Not "Friend?"

529
00:21:05,807 --> 00:21:09,306
(So he watched "Damo" instead of "Friend.")

530
00:21:09,307 --> 00:21:10,837
It's because...

531
00:21:11,377 --> 00:21:14,807
When you live abroad, you get homesick.

532
00:21:15,747 --> 00:21:17,877
Back then, I used to go to Koreatown...

533
00:21:18,177 --> 00:21:20,046
- and rent videotapes.
- You rented videotapes?

534
00:21:20,047 --> 00:21:21,117
That's how I...

535
00:21:21,287 --> 00:21:22,686
So you watched "Damo" on VHS.

536
00:21:22,687 --> 00:21:24,586
Yes, I rented "Damo."

537
00:21:24,587 --> 00:21:26,656
(When he was studying abroad, he watched "Damo" on VHS.)

538
00:21:26,657 --> 00:21:29,556
- That was...
- Ha Ji Won and Seo Jin.

539
00:21:29,557 --> 00:21:31,627
Yes. I'll never forget it.

540
00:21:33,597 --> 00:21:37,566
(Does it hurt?)

541
00:21:37,567 --> 00:21:39,407
(It hurts me too.)

542
00:21:40,167 --> 00:21:42,236
("Damo," the all-time favorite drama not just for My Star,)

543
00:21:42,237 --> 00:21:43,476
(but countless others)

544
00:21:43,477 --> 00:21:46,577
(The iconic shot of these two that made Suk Ku's heart flutter)

545
00:21:47,377 --> 00:21:48,646
Why are you in a hurry?

546
00:21:48,647 --> 00:21:49,746
(A few days later at Incheon International Airport)

547
00:21:49,747 --> 00:21:51,017
I don't want to find it.

548
00:21:51,847 --> 00:21:53,017
I feel sick.

549
00:21:53,217 --> 00:21:54,416
I need to go to the restroom.

550
00:21:54,417 --> 00:21:55,756
- Seo Jin.
- Ji Won.

551
00:21:55,757 --> 00:21:56,957
(Seo Jin!)

552
00:21:57,517 --> 00:22:00,327
(Ji Won!)

553
00:22:04,497 --> 00:22:10,037
(Next week, we'll finally get another shot of the two of them.)

554
00:22:11,597 --> 00:22:14,737
I loved "Damo." When I was living in the US,

555
00:22:15,537 --> 00:22:17,977
Blockbuster stores were still around.

556
00:22:18,207 --> 00:22:20,106
I practically lived there.

557
00:22:20,107 --> 00:22:22,447
I'd rent 2 or 3 movies a day and watch them all.

558
00:22:22,677 --> 00:22:26,817
Going to Blockbuster was part of my daily routine back then.

559
00:22:27,387 --> 00:22:29,856
- It's so fun.
- It's so fun there.

560
00:22:29,857 --> 00:22:32,387
I was always hanging out...

561
00:22:33,157 --> 00:22:34,157
in the international section.

562
00:22:34,158 --> 00:22:35,186
(Seo Jin has many things in common with My Star.)

563
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:37,027
I loved watching the DVDs I rented from there.

564
00:22:38,997 --> 00:22:39,997
It was part of my daily routine.

565
00:22:39,998 --> 00:22:42,336
(He gets left out when they start talking about America.)

566
00:22:42,337 --> 00:22:47,267
(Touching the fan for no reason)

567
00:22:47,937 --> 00:22:49,676
Watching "Uncle Vanya..."

568
00:22:49,677 --> 00:22:50,906
made me think about a lot of things.

569
00:22:50,907 --> 00:22:52,077
That's so random.

570
00:22:52,707 --> 00:22:53,906
Why are you suddenly talking about "Uncle Vanya?"

571
00:22:53,907 --> 00:22:54,907
I'm serious.

572
00:22:54,908 --> 00:22:57,617
I watched "Uncle Vanya" with my friends.

573
00:22:58,317 --> 00:23:00,746
I felt a sense of catharsis watching it.

574
00:23:00,747 --> 00:23:04,616
That made me see Seo Jin in a whole new light...

575
00:23:04,617 --> 00:23:07,256
even though I'd seen a lot of his work.

576
00:23:07,257 --> 00:23:08,326
(My Star suddenly starts praising him.)

577
00:23:08,327 --> 00:23:11,957
I felt a weird sense of catharsis.

578
00:23:12,097 --> 00:23:14,526
How many months did you rehearse for it?

579
00:23:14,527 --> 00:23:15,866
- Two months.
- Two months?

580
00:23:15,867 --> 00:23:19,207
Yes. I didn't miss a single rehearsal.

581
00:23:20,307 --> 00:23:22,276
I want to do something like that too.

582
00:23:22,277 --> 00:23:23,576
(This is not what I was thinking about.)

583
00:23:23,577 --> 00:23:25,237
That character is just like him in real life.

584
00:23:26,077 --> 00:23:29,447
When you get there, you'll see another actor,

585
00:23:29,677 --> 00:23:30,847
Choi Hee Seo.

586
00:23:31,217 --> 00:23:34,987
Hee Seo and I have been friends for a very long time.

587
00:23:35,147 --> 00:23:36,786
Even before you became an actor?

588
00:23:36,787 --> 00:23:38,557
Well...

589
00:23:38,827 --> 00:23:42,297
I still do everything she says.

590
00:23:42,997 --> 00:23:45,296
Things always worked out well for me when I listened to her.

591
00:23:45,297 --> 00:23:47,166
Is there any case that you got a role...

592
00:23:47,167 --> 00:23:49,036
after she told you to go for an audition?

593
00:23:49,037 --> 00:23:50,896
She filmed...

594
00:23:50,897 --> 00:23:52,706
Was it "Dongju: The Portrait of a Poet?"

595
00:23:52,707 --> 00:23:53,736
She filmed a movie named something like that.

596
00:23:53,737 --> 00:23:54,866
She filmed it. Yes.

597
00:23:54,867 --> 00:23:55,906
When she became known...

598
00:23:55,907 --> 00:23:56,907
- to the public for that...
- Right.

599
00:23:56,908 --> 00:23:58,406
and won Best Actress...

600
00:23:58,407 --> 00:23:59,876
- It was all over the news.
- Yes.

601
00:23:59,877 --> 00:24:02,076
I was watching it all from home.

602
00:24:02,077 --> 00:24:03,376
So she made it first.

603
00:24:03,377 --> 00:24:04,617
She became very successful.

604
00:24:05,377 --> 00:24:06,447
One day, she said,

605
00:24:06,887 --> 00:24:08,517
"Don't stay at home like that."

606
00:24:08,817 --> 00:24:10,716
"Do you have 1,000 dollars?"

607
00:24:10,717 --> 00:24:13,526
"If you do, let's save up 3,000 dollars..."

608
00:24:13,527 --> 00:24:17,357
"and put on a play."

609
00:24:17,927 --> 00:24:19,426
So we did.

610
00:24:19,427 --> 00:24:23,266
She didn't put on the play for a public audience.

611
00:24:23,267 --> 00:24:26,707
Instead, she created it as a showcase...

612
00:24:26,967 --> 00:24:29,476
for industry professionals she'd met while making films...

613
00:24:29,477 --> 00:24:30,807
and invited them to come see it.

614
00:24:31,037 --> 00:24:32,476
- She's smart.
- She's very smart.

615
00:24:32,477 --> 00:24:34,206
- She's extremely smart.
- Yes.

616
00:24:34,207 --> 00:24:36,747
Who would've thought of it?

617
00:24:37,747 --> 00:24:40,246
After that, the casting director...

618
00:24:40,247 --> 00:24:43,057
for "Sense8," the series I mentioned earlier,

619
00:24:43,157 --> 00:24:45,057
came to the showcase and cast me.

620
00:24:46,757 --> 00:24:48,626
- You owe her.
- I owe her.

621
00:24:48,627 --> 00:24:50,527
I feel so grateful to her.

622
00:24:50,597 --> 00:24:53,066
At first, I wasn't going...

623
00:24:53,067 --> 00:24:55,996
to audition for "Sense8,"

624
00:24:55,997 --> 00:24:57,636
but she scolded me...

625
00:24:57,637 --> 00:24:59,707
and insisted I go because she had a good feeling about it.

626
00:25:00,137 --> 00:25:02,176
She has a good instinct.

627
00:25:02,177 --> 00:25:03,376
(He was going to give up, but she put him in his place.)

628
00:25:03,377 --> 00:25:06,106
- She's like your manager.
- Yes. So...

629
00:25:06,107 --> 00:25:08,847
- I followed her and...
- You should get close to her.

630
00:25:09,077 --> 00:25:10,816
I need to make a good impression on her today.

631
00:25:10,817 --> 00:25:12,076
You should.

632
00:25:12,077 --> 00:25:14,317
- She really has a good instinct.
- Right. I should.

633
00:25:15,047 --> 00:25:18,957
(Stage greeting coming up shortly)

634
00:25:19,587 --> 00:25:22,126
(The only actor I feel truly grateful to...)

635
00:25:22,127 --> 00:25:23,826
(is Hee Seo.)

636
00:25:23,827 --> 00:25:27,796
(To me, Hee Seo...)

637
00:25:27,797 --> 00:25:29,366
That's why I did this.

638
00:25:29,367 --> 00:25:33,337
(What shocking statement did he make that left everyone stunned?)

639
00:25:34,837 --> 00:25:37,376
There was a program in Busan...

640
00:25:37,377 --> 00:25:40,246
that discovered new actors.

641
00:25:40,247 --> 00:25:42,616
It was a project aimed at finding 5 to 7 newcomers...

642
00:25:42,617 --> 00:25:44,977
and turning them into stars across Asia.

643
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:47,187
Hee Seo and I were both selected.

644
00:25:48,687 --> 00:25:50,087
It was quite a moment,

645
00:25:50,257 --> 00:25:51,886
coming to BIFF together after more than a decade...

646
00:25:51,887 --> 00:25:53,486
after having worked together on a film.

647
00:25:53,487 --> 00:25:54,857
(15 years later, they came to Busan International Film Festival.)

648
00:25:55,487 --> 00:25:57,456
(My Star, Choi Hee Seo)

649
00:25:57,457 --> 00:25:59,496
(The two ambitious newcomers...)

650
00:25:59,497 --> 00:26:01,466
- So...
- You became superstars.

651
00:26:01,467 --> 00:26:04,536
(have become established stars, proudly representing Korea at BIFF.)

652
00:26:04,537 --> 00:26:05,936
- It...
- It brings back memories.

653
00:26:05,937 --> 00:26:07,737
- It brings back memories.
- Yes.

654
00:26:07,937 --> 00:26:09,207
I feel grateful.

655
00:26:10,207 --> 00:26:11,476
(They arrive at BIFF, which holds even greater meaning for My Star.)

656
00:26:11,477 --> 00:26:13,607
We're here.

657
00:26:14,777 --> 00:26:16,246
What are you doing here?

658
00:26:16,247 --> 00:26:17,447
We...

659
00:26:17,717 --> 00:26:18,916
What's "outdoor stage greeting?"

660
00:26:18,917 --> 00:26:22,856
- We'll greet the audience here...
- Yes.

661
00:26:22,857 --> 00:26:24,057
and watch the movie together.

662
00:26:24,787 --> 00:26:27,527
(A grand scale)

663
00:26:28,827 --> 00:26:35,197
(It hosts the red-carpet events, the highlight of the film festival,)

664
00:26:37,837 --> 00:26:40,666
(featuring an outdoor theater where audiences can enjoy films.)

665
00:26:40,667 --> 00:26:43,937
(The stage My Star will take)

666
00:26:44,477 --> 00:26:47,807
(A BIFF landmark...)

667
00:26:48,277 --> 00:26:51,846
(where the festival's major events take place)

668
00:26:51,847 --> 00:26:53,617
What are we eating?

669
00:26:54,787 --> 00:26:55,886
What do you want?

670
00:26:55,887 --> 00:26:57,556
Kwang Kyu, on our way there...

671
00:26:57,557 --> 00:26:58,586
(My Star asked him to choose what to have for lunch.)

672
00:26:58,587 --> 00:26:59,686
Hold on. From here...

673
00:26:59,687 --> 00:27:00,756
(Since we're on a tight schedule...)

674
00:27:00,757 --> 00:27:02,896
We could go to the restaurant area in Centum...

675
00:27:02,897 --> 00:27:03,957
- What?
- Would it be too crowded?

676
00:27:04,027 --> 00:27:05,196
- There are lots of nice places.
- It's nearby.

677
00:27:05,197 --> 00:27:06,767
They're all near here.

678
00:27:07,267 --> 00:27:08,426
Do you want to go to Centum?

679
00:27:08,427 --> 00:27:10,437
- That sounds good.
- Centum is a good place.

680
00:27:10,537 --> 00:27:11,637
Okay.

681
00:27:11,867 --> 00:27:13,937
What should we eat?

682
00:27:14,537 --> 00:27:16,706
There are dozens of things to eat there.

683
00:27:16,707 --> 00:27:18,177
They would have all sorts of delicious food.

684
00:27:18,237 --> 00:27:19,776
Are you going to ask them on the spot?

685
00:27:19,777 --> 00:27:21,077
Yes.

686
00:27:21,607 --> 00:27:23,246
Centum? I've been there before.

687
00:27:23,247 --> 00:27:24,277
(Charmed by Seo Genie's initiative)

688
00:27:24,517 --> 00:27:26,746
(They first head to the waiting room.)

689
00:27:26,747 --> 00:27:28,886
The producers of this movie...

690
00:27:28,887 --> 00:27:31,487
are all Americans.

691
00:27:31,787 --> 00:27:33,386
- Even the director.
- For "Bedford Park?"

692
00:27:33,387 --> 00:27:34,526
Yes.

693
00:27:34,527 --> 00:27:35,527
So we'll be hearing...

694
00:27:35,527 --> 00:27:36,527
- you speak English.
- Gosh.

695
00:27:36,597 --> 00:27:37,796
This...

696
00:27:37,797 --> 00:27:39,196
(I'll get to hear Seo Jin talk in English.)

697
00:27:39,197 --> 00:27:41,066
So do you say the lines in English as well?

698
00:27:41,067 --> 00:27:42,266
They're all...

699
00:27:42,267 --> 00:27:43,336
- They're all in English?
- Yes.

700
00:27:43,337 --> 00:27:44,736
This...

701
00:27:44,737 --> 00:27:46,306
is the first feature film we produced...

702
00:27:46,307 --> 00:27:48,037
after starting our company.

703
00:27:48,507 --> 00:27:50,237
- You produced it?
- Yes.

704
00:27:51,037 --> 00:27:52,877
- All in English?
- Yes.

705
00:27:52,947 --> 00:27:54,807
- Seriously.
- We filmed this in New Jersey.

706
00:27:54,877 --> 00:27:56,047
- Really?
- Yes.

707
00:27:56,577 --> 00:27:59,016
(Seriously...)

708
00:27:59,017 --> 00:28:00,647
You're really global.

709
00:28:01,517 --> 00:28:03,287
I just go to the US for vacation.

710
00:28:03,417 --> 00:28:04,817
You go there to work.

711
00:28:05,617 --> 00:28:06,887
I've seen that show.

712
00:28:06,957 --> 00:28:08,526
- What show?
- "Ready or Not: Texas."

713
00:28:08,527 --> 00:28:09,797
- "Ready or Not: Texas?"
- Yes.

714
00:28:10,157 --> 00:28:12,366
(I watched your show.)

715
00:28:12,367 --> 00:28:15,327
(Did you forget about me, Suk Ku?)

716
00:28:15,867 --> 00:28:16,867
Have you been to Texas?

717
00:28:16,868 --> 00:28:18,096
Not yet. I want to go there.

718
00:28:18,097 --> 00:28:19,806
- Texas is nice.
- My friend lives in Texas.

719
00:28:19,807 --> 00:28:20,866
- Really?
- Yes.

720
00:28:20,867 --> 00:28:22,066
Texas is really nice.

721
00:28:22,067 --> 00:28:23,376
This...

722
00:28:23,377 --> 00:28:25,137
is where I came before.

723
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:27,646
Where? Did you get makeup here?

724
00:28:27,647 --> 00:28:28,676
The one I mentioned before.

725
00:28:28,677 --> 00:28:29,716
When...

726
00:28:29,717 --> 00:28:32,347
- I see.
- the actors were cast...

727
00:28:32,517 --> 00:28:34,286
I auditioned here.

728
00:28:34,287 --> 00:28:35,347
Really?

729
00:28:35,387 --> 00:28:36,756
This was where you auditioned...

730
00:28:36,757 --> 00:28:38,417
and got picked?

731
00:28:39,327 --> 00:28:40,526
I see.

732
00:28:40,527 --> 00:28:41,756
(Staring)

733
00:28:41,757 --> 00:28:42,997
I...

734
00:28:43,027 --> 00:28:44,857
It feels so new.

735
00:28:45,397 --> 00:28:47,127
When Hee Seo comes here...

736
00:28:47,927 --> 00:28:50,097
We were so nervous here...

737
00:28:50,237 --> 00:28:52,336
"Applicant 52, Son Suk Ku, you're next."

738
00:28:52,337 --> 00:28:54,306
This is where we waited together.

739
00:28:54,307 --> 00:28:56,137
(The place he waited for his turn at the audition with Hee Seo)

740
00:28:56,777 --> 00:28:57,836
He...

741
00:28:57,837 --> 00:28:59,046
He has lots of fun old stories.

742
00:28:59,047 --> 00:29:00,377
It's an old story.

743
00:29:00,707 --> 00:29:02,517
You became a star.

744
00:29:03,047 --> 00:29:04,077
Right.

745
00:29:04,677 --> 00:29:06,987
(Someone appeared.)

746
00:29:07,017 --> 00:29:09,757
(Who is it?)

747
00:29:10,157 --> 00:29:11,256
Our director.

748
00:29:11,257 --> 00:29:12,526
We should greet her.

749
00:29:12,527 --> 00:29:13,686
(Stephanie Ahn, director of "Bedford Park")

750
00:29:13,687 --> 00:29:15,027
Do I sit here?

751
00:29:15,157 --> 00:29:17,697
We're filming My Genie Secretary.

752
00:29:17,857 --> 00:29:20,696
We're working...

753
00:29:20,697 --> 00:29:24,137
as Son Suk Ku's managers.

754
00:29:24,467 --> 00:29:25,906
Please make yourself comfortable.

755
00:29:25,907 --> 00:29:27,237
(Why is he suddenly acting like that?)

756
00:29:27,607 --> 00:29:28,866
Just a moment. I'll...

757
00:29:28,867 --> 00:29:30,207
(He shows off his gentlemanly side by pulling out her chair.)

758
00:29:30,507 --> 00:29:32,647
- Hello.
- So this is...

759
00:29:33,347 --> 00:29:36,176
(Seo Jin also greets her.)

760
00:29:36,177 --> 00:29:37,416
- They're my seniors.
- Yes.

761
00:29:37,417 --> 00:29:39,287
- Hello.
- Lee Seo Jin.

762
00:29:39,347 --> 00:29:41,217
- Kim Kwang Kyu.
- Hello.

763
00:29:41,517 --> 00:29:45,987
It's a TV show...

764
00:29:46,157 --> 00:29:47,687
promoting our film.

765
00:29:48,127 --> 00:29:49,326
You can watch it...

766
00:29:49,327 --> 00:29:50,526
- on a streaming service.
- This show?

767
00:29:50,527 --> 00:29:51,996
- But only in Korea.
- Through a streaming service.

768
00:29:51,997 --> 00:29:53,527
- Only in Korea? Okay.
- Yes.

769
00:29:53,597 --> 00:29:55,596
So this was a scheduled thing that you...

770
00:29:55,597 --> 00:29:57,667
- It was a scheduled thing.
- Okay.

771
00:29:57,737 --> 00:30:00,036
So they're going to be with me the whole day today.

772
00:30:00,037 --> 00:30:01,407
I see.

773
00:30:01,837 --> 00:30:05,637
I have a new TV series coming out.

774
00:30:06,007 --> 00:30:08,546
(My Star communicates with fluent English.)

775
00:30:08,547 --> 00:30:09,647
What's the title?

776
00:30:10,117 --> 00:30:12,117
This is Stephanie Ahn.

777
00:30:12,247 --> 00:30:15,117
She's our movie's director, born and raised in Brooklyn.

778
00:30:15,447 --> 00:30:16,787
I went to high school in Brooklyn.

779
00:30:17,457 --> 00:30:18,887
I went to high school in Brooklyn.

780
00:30:20,327 --> 00:30:22,257
- You're from Brooklyn?
- Yes. High school.

781
00:30:22,357 --> 00:30:23,827
- Where?
- Saint Ann's.

782
00:30:24,157 --> 00:30:25,356
- You went to Saint Ann's?
- Yes.

783
00:30:25,357 --> 00:30:26,666
