1046
00:41:04,837 --> 00:41:06,707
But I think we click quite well.

1047
00:41:09,167 --> 00:41:13,407
(Time: 12pm, Location: Department store dining area, Details: Lunch)

1048
00:41:14,877 --> 00:41:16,046
- Enjoy your meal.
- Okay.

1049
00:41:16,047 --> 00:41:17,246
Thank you.

1050
00:41:17,247 --> 00:41:18,277
(They get to the dining area for lunch.)

1051
00:41:20,017 --> 00:41:22,746
We have to make a quick decision.

1052
00:41:22,747 --> 00:41:24,786
- How should we do it?
- Take a look around.

1053
00:41:24,787 --> 00:41:25,857
Shall we do that?

1054
00:41:26,927 --> 00:41:29,186
They had stone pot bibimbap as well.

1055
00:41:29,187 --> 00:41:31,757
- Don't say what you want to eat.
- I'm just saying.

1056
00:41:32,297 --> 00:41:34,927
I eat almost everything,

1057
00:41:35,267 --> 00:41:36,536
but I can't eat stone pot bibimbap...

1058
00:41:36,537 --> 00:41:37,797
- because it's hot.
- Really?

1059
00:41:38,367 --> 00:41:40,607
(It's not working out well with My Star.)

1060
00:41:41,467 --> 00:41:44,077
(Looking around)

1061
00:41:45,807 --> 00:41:48,277
(Running)

1062
00:41:48,647 --> 00:41:52,447
You can choose what you want, My Star.

1063
00:41:52,647 --> 00:41:55,517
(Carefully choosing the menu)

1064
00:41:56,287 --> 00:41:58,956
All the good restaurants are here.

1065
00:41:58,957 --> 00:41:59,957
(What does My Star want for lunch?)

1066
00:42:00,857 --> 00:42:02,456
Dishes that make you sweat and ruin the makeup...

1067
00:42:02,457 --> 00:42:04,996
I like naengmyeon...

1068
00:42:04,997 --> 00:42:07,267
- Naengmyeon, Chinese food, - Yes.

1069
00:42:07,467 --> 00:42:09,366
and sushi. That's what I like.

1070
00:42:09,367 --> 00:42:10,696
That's all.

1071
00:42:10,697 --> 00:42:11,836
What about Hee Seo?

1072
00:42:11,837 --> 00:42:12,837
(This is difficult.)

1073
00:42:14,067 --> 00:42:15,666
- Seo Jin...
- Shall we have some sushi?

1074
00:42:15,667 --> 00:42:16,676
- What do you think?
- That sounds great.

1075
00:42:16,677 --> 00:42:17,736
Shall we have some sushi?

1076
00:42:17,737 --> 00:42:19,006
- Okay.
- Yes. I'd love that.

1077
00:42:19,007 --> 00:42:20,647
- Okay.
- Let's go.

1078
00:42:21,007 --> 00:42:24,047
(The super-efficient secretary's quick thinking)

1079
00:42:24,717 --> 00:42:26,376
We're going to this restaurant.

1080
00:42:26,377 --> 00:42:27,417
(They all head to the sushi restaurant.)

1081
00:42:27,547 --> 00:42:30,156
(Running)

1082
00:42:30,157 --> 00:42:32,717
Hello. We're from My Genie Secretary.

1083
00:42:32,887 --> 00:42:35,527
Would it be okay to film us having lunch with Son Suk Ku?

1084
00:42:36,287 --> 00:42:37,397
- Hold on a minute.
- Okay.

1085
00:42:37,727 --> 00:42:39,966
- Would it be okay?
- Yes.

1086
00:42:39,967 --> 00:42:41,666
Yes. Are there seats?

1087
00:42:41,667 --> 00:42:42,726
(He's a pro at scouting locations now.)

1088
00:42:42,727 --> 00:42:44,296
- This would be enough.
- It's big enough.

1089
00:42:44,297 --> 00:42:46,197
- It's great.
- Is it okay?

1090
00:42:47,067 --> 00:42:48,506
- Sit inside.
- Inside?

1091
00:42:48,507 --> 00:42:51,307
(They lead My Star to the best seat.)

1092
00:42:53,347 --> 00:42:56,447
(They check the menu first.)

1093
00:42:56,847 --> 00:42:58,746
(Let me see.)

1094
00:42:58,747 --> 00:43:02,116
I should get eel over rice.

1095
00:43:02,117 --> 00:43:03,146
(His mouth is watering.)

1096
00:43:03,147 --> 00:43:04,257
A large eel over rice.

1097
00:43:05,287 --> 00:43:06,386
Seaweed soup?

1098
00:43:06,387 --> 00:43:08,526
(My Star was very hungry.)

1099
00:43:08,527 --> 00:43:10,897
I'll get this...

1100
00:43:11,197 --> 00:43:13,296
and ask how much seaweed soup they serve,

1101
00:43:13,297 --> 00:43:14,927
and if it's not so much, I'll get this as well.

1102
00:43:15,497 --> 00:43:18,967
They wouldn't serve so little. It's a dish on its own.

1103
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:21,506
- Eel over rice.
- Eel over rice? Which size?

1104
00:43:21,507 --> 00:43:22,936
- The course menu, large, or small?
- He wants a large one.

1105
00:43:22,937 --> 00:43:24,537
- Large?
- Eel over rice? Large.

1106
00:43:25,037 --> 00:43:27,507
- It's 150g.
- He eats well.

1107
00:43:27,847 --> 00:43:30,277
Okay. Like that.

1108
00:43:30,947 --> 00:43:33,487
This is nice. I love the menu.

1109
00:43:34,447 --> 00:43:38,057
You really don't age.

1110
00:43:39,287 --> 00:43:40,557
You look really young.

1111
00:43:41,387 --> 00:43:43,056
When I filmed "Friend," I was...

1112
00:43:43,057 --> 00:43:44,697
He looks the same as when he filmed that film.

1113
00:43:44,927 --> 00:43:46,456
He lost a lot of hair.

1114
00:43:46,457 --> 00:43:47,627
He didn't have so much even then.

1115
00:43:48,167 --> 00:43:49,226
(No offense intended)

1116
00:43:49,227 --> 00:43:51,266
- It wasn't this bad.
- It wasn't this bad.

1117
00:43:51,267 --> 00:43:52,297
(Glancing)

1118
00:43:52,467 --> 00:43:53,707
- Really?
- Yes.

1119
00:43:54,467 --> 00:43:55,807
(A coy look)

1120
00:43:56,137 --> 00:43:57,137
- Now...
- But...

1121
00:43:57,138 --> 00:43:58,437
- His skin...
- He looks like he's 100 days old.

1122
00:43:59,277 --> 00:44:00,847
- That's mean.
- Right?

1123
00:44:01,007 --> 00:44:03,107
He's Benjamin. He's 100 days old.

1124
00:44:03,617 --> 00:44:05,216
Last year, he was one year old.

1125
00:44:05,217 --> 00:44:06,276
He was...

1126
00:44:06,277 --> 00:44:07,747
(They get each other's humor as well.)

1127
00:44:08,147 --> 00:44:09,616
- Yes.
- Here's the sushi.

1128
00:44:09,617 --> 00:44:11,086
Here, please.

1129
00:44:11,087 --> 00:44:13,157
- Eel...
- Sushi.

1130
00:44:13,387 --> 00:44:15,056
I ordered eel over rice.

1131
00:44:15,057 --> 00:44:16,186
(From sushi packed with the flavors of Busan's waters...)

1132
00:44:16,187 --> 00:44:17,726
Try the tuna.

1133
00:44:17,727 --> 00:44:18,896
Have some, My Star.

1134
00:44:18,897 --> 00:44:20,726
- I'll have my dish.
- You can feel free to have some.

1135
00:44:20,727 --> 00:44:21,826
It's a lot.

1136
00:44:21,827 --> 00:44:23,736
Thank you.

1137
00:44:23,737 --> 00:44:25,097
Enjoy your meal.

1138
00:44:25,137 --> 00:44:27,207
Yes. Thank you.

1139
00:44:28,067 --> 00:44:30,076
(Thank you for the meal.)

1140
00:44:30,077 --> 00:44:32,807
(Taking a large bite of the eel over rice)

1141
00:44:37,217 --> 00:44:39,646
(Taking a big bite of the urchin roe as well)

1142
00:44:39,647 --> 00:44:40,717
It's so good.

1143
00:44:40,817 --> 00:44:41,917
Yes.

1144
00:44:43,387 --> 00:44:45,257
(Exclaiming)

1145
00:44:45,817 --> 00:44:49,327
(My Star is eating well.)

1146
00:44:50,457 --> 00:44:53,626
This is quite random,

1147
00:44:53,627 --> 00:44:56,027
but I was in New Jersey when I was in high school.

1148
00:44:56,667 --> 00:44:59,496
The H Mart there now...

1149
00:44:59,497 --> 00:45:01,266
- used to be Hanareum Mart.
- Hanareum.

1150
00:45:01,267 --> 00:45:02,906
There was a video store there.

1151
00:45:02,907 --> 00:45:03,936
There was.

1152
00:45:03,937 --> 00:45:05,836
I went through the entire series...

1153
00:45:05,837 --> 00:45:07,546
- of "Damo."
- "Damo" again?

1154
00:45:07,547 --> 00:45:09,146
I went through the entire series of "Damo."

1155
00:45:09,147 --> 00:45:10,817
"Damo" again?

1156
00:45:10,917 --> 00:45:12,846
I already said that earlier.

1157
00:45:12,847 --> 00:45:14,646
You did? Let me talk about it.

1158
00:45:14,647 --> 00:45:16,187
Because I...

1159
00:45:16,387 --> 00:45:17,816
("Damo" again?)

1160
00:45:17,817 --> 00:45:19,087
"Damo."

1161
00:45:19,787 --> 00:45:22,057
(His excited dimples)

1162
00:45:22,227 --> 00:45:25,026
That was a drama I watched...

1163
00:45:25,027 --> 00:45:27,466
and really thought I should become an actress.

1164
00:45:27,467 --> 00:45:28,496
- Really?
- There was "Damo..."

1165
00:45:28,497 --> 00:45:30,537
and "Peppermint Candy" by Lee Chang Dong.

1166
00:45:31,197 --> 00:45:32,467
I watched those two...

1167
00:45:33,297 --> 00:45:35,267
and really fell for them.

1168
00:45:36,137 --> 00:45:38,006
- But "Damo" was really...
- It was amazing.

1169
00:45:38,007 --> 00:45:39,936
- heartbreaking.
- I loved it.

1170
00:45:39,937 --> 00:45:41,607
- The love story.
- That's right.

1171
00:45:42,377 --> 00:45:44,177
(Feeling proud)

1172
00:45:44,977 --> 00:45:46,746
Did you think...

1173
00:45:46,747 --> 00:45:50,117
it would do so well when you filmed it?

1174
00:45:50,217 --> 00:45:52,217
- Wasn't it...
- I never thought it would do well.

1175
00:45:52,287 --> 00:45:54,357
- You thought it would do just okay?
- I understand.

1176
00:45:54,687 --> 00:45:57,757
But after the first episode...

1177
00:45:58,727 --> 00:45:59,756
I said it earlier.

1178
00:45:59,757 --> 00:46:02,996
The world was a different place every morning.

1179
00:46:02,997 --> 00:46:05,097
- I see.
- "Damo" was like that.

1180
00:46:06,267 --> 00:46:07,406
Every day was different.

1181
00:46:07,407 --> 00:46:08,707
("Damo" made Seo Jin a star.)

1182
00:46:10,007 --> 00:46:12,536
(That's how the masterpiece that broke the hearts...)

1183
00:46:12,537 --> 00:46:14,507
(of the entire nation was born.)

1184
00:46:15,277 --> 00:46:19,247
He's normally very shy,

1185
00:46:19,617 --> 00:46:23,146
but when he starts talking to someone in a group,

1186
00:46:23,147 --> 00:46:26,457
he talks to that person very deeply.

1187
00:46:26,517 --> 00:46:28,756
- He seems like it.
- Then people start...

1188
00:46:28,757 --> 00:46:32,457
gathering around him. It's quite interesting.

1189
00:46:32,657 --> 00:46:34,567
He also has many stories about his life.

1190
00:46:35,467 --> 00:46:37,597
- Right.
- He has many stories.

1191
00:46:37,897 --> 00:46:40,537
How did you end up getting deployed to Iraq?

1192
00:46:41,637 --> 00:46:42,807
- Me?
- Yes.

1193
00:46:46,007 --> 00:46:50,777
(My Star's story: Deployed to Iraq with the Zaytun Division)

1194
00:46:51,417 --> 00:46:53,146
Did your father tell you to do it?

1195
00:46:53,147 --> 00:46:55,917
Or was it your decision?

1196
00:46:56,287 --> 00:47:00,487
I wanted to go to Iraq.

1197
00:47:01,257 --> 00:47:04,857
You have to volunteer.

1198
00:47:06,397 --> 00:47:08,966
And in order to do that, you need your parents to stamp it.

1199
00:47:08,967 --> 00:47:10,197
- Really?
- Yes.

1200
00:47:10,837 --> 00:47:13,836
I was...

1201
00:47:13,837 --> 00:47:15,966
serving in the army headquarters at the time.

1202
00:47:15,967 --> 00:47:18,607
There was a stamp place inside.

1203
00:47:19,377 --> 00:47:22,677
I forged my parents' stamps.

1204
00:47:23,447 --> 00:47:25,317
So you didn't get your parents' approval?

1205
00:47:25,647 --> 00:47:27,647
(You didn't ask for their approval?)

1206
00:47:27,887 --> 00:47:29,886
After I made it,

1207
00:47:29,887 --> 00:47:33,357
I told my parents that I forged their stamps.

1208
00:47:33,457 --> 00:47:36,586
"If I confess it now, I'll be sent to the guardhouse."

1209
00:47:36,587 --> 00:47:38,527
I told them I had no choice but to go.

1210
00:47:38,997 --> 00:47:40,566
- Because...
- Gosh.

1211
00:47:40,567 --> 00:47:43,896
I told them I wanted to go with the previous batch,

1212
00:47:43,897 --> 00:47:44,897
but they said no.

1213
00:47:45,337 --> 00:47:47,607
So I had to come up with a new strategy.

1214
00:47:48,007 --> 00:47:49,336
- You got their stamps first.
- Yes.

1215
00:47:49,337 --> 00:47:52,136
I still can't forget...

1216
00:47:52,137 --> 00:47:53,806
my dad's sigh on the phone.

1217
00:47:53,807 --> 00:47:55,277
It was really deep.

1218
00:47:58,347 --> 00:47:59,516
(No wonder.)

1219
00:47:59,517 --> 00:48:00,517
What else?

1220
00:48:00,917 --> 00:48:02,387
I had to go.

1221
00:48:03,657 --> 00:48:05,916
What was the reason you wanted to go so badly...

1222
00:48:05,917 --> 00:48:07,427
that you even forged their stamps?

1223
00:48:09,187 --> 00:48:10,996
- To be deployed in Iraq.
- Me?

1224
00:48:10,997 --> 00:48:12,157
- I...
- Yes?

1225
00:48:12,997 --> 00:48:15,667
lived in the States for a long time without visiting Korea.

1226
00:48:16,597 --> 00:48:18,397
Then just a month or two after I got into the university,

1227
00:48:19,497 --> 00:48:22,107
I joined the army.

1228
00:48:22,467 --> 00:48:25,606
It was really hard to get used to it.

1229
00:48:25,607 --> 00:48:27,906
(Unlike his life in the US,)

1230
00:48:27,907 --> 00:48:34,147
(everything in the army was new.)

1231
00:48:34,317 --> 00:48:36,717
I couldn't even speak Korean that well at the time.

1232
00:48:37,357 --> 00:48:39,117
- When I joined the army like that, - You must've...

1233
00:48:40,187 --> 00:48:43,526
what should I call it?

1234
00:48:43,527 --> 00:48:45,257
My survival instinct...

1235
00:48:45,727 --> 00:48:47,367
(Survival what?)

1236
00:48:47,667 --> 00:48:49,827
He doesn't know what survival instinct means.

1237
00:48:50,237 --> 00:48:52,436
(No one looks after Kwang Kyu like Seo Jin does.)

1238
00:48:52,437 --> 00:48:55,036
- I'm sorry, but...
- What's it called?

1239
00:48:55,037 --> 00:48:56,106
My bad.

1240
00:48:56,107 --> 00:48:59,677
My survival instinct told me...

1241
00:48:59,837 --> 00:49:04,877
I must do my best here to blend in.

1242
00:49:05,017 --> 00:49:07,116
- If not, - You wouldn't be able to blend it.

1243
00:49:07,117 --> 00:49:09,247
I wouldn't be able to blend in.

1244
00:49:09,717 --> 00:49:12,386
- So...
- You didn't sound normal either.

1245
00:49:12,387 --> 00:49:13,826
I got in so much trouble.

1246
00:49:13,827 --> 00:49:15,787
"Why do you talk like that? Why do you walk like that?"

1247
00:49:16,187 --> 00:49:17,557
"You think you're a rapper?"

1248
00:49:17,727 --> 00:49:19,457
I kept getting criticized.

1249
00:49:19,627 --> 00:49:23,196
You go to a religious service on weekends,

1250
00:49:23,197 --> 00:49:24,437
and you clap.

1251
00:49:24,997 --> 00:49:28,907
And I grew up listening to MTV hip-hop.

1252
00:49:29,137 --> 00:49:30,976
I got in trouble for the way I clap.

1253
00:49:30,977 --> 00:49:32,337
- You...
- I clapped like a rapper.

1254
00:49:32,677 --> 00:49:33,976
- Did you have the vibe?
- Yes.

1255
00:49:33,977 --> 00:49:36,206
So...

1256
00:49:36,207 --> 00:49:38,747
In order to break through,

1257
00:49:39,417 --> 00:49:41,516
I worked so hard as a trainee.

1258
00:49:41,517 --> 00:49:45,986
So I completed my training at the top of my batch.

1259
00:49:45,987 --> 00:49:47,486
(As a result)

1260
00:49:47,487 --> 00:49:49,326
- You mean the top.
- Yes.

1261
00:49:49,327 --> 00:49:51,027
When I was young,

1262
00:49:51,157 --> 00:49:53,967
I wanted to...

1263
00:49:54,127 --> 00:49:57,637
go as far as I could as a soldier.

1264
00:50:01,037 --> 00:50:02,507
Did that happen when you were a private?

1265
00:50:03,107 --> 00:50:05,076
I missed my chance when I was a private.

1266
00:50:05,077 --> 00:50:06,806
Then when I was a private first class,

1267
00:50:06,807 --> 00:50:08,606
- A private first class, - I applied.

1268
00:50:08,607 --> 00:50:09,607
(He made it when he was a private first class.)

1269
00:50:09,747 --> 00:50:11,816
(Exclaiming)

1270
00:50:11,817 --> 00:50:12,877
That's amazing.

1271
00:50:13,247 --> 00:50:14,347
What was your assignment?

1272
00:50:15,017 --> 00:50:17,017
I was a rifleman.

1273
00:50:18,087 --> 00:50:19,717
But since I could translate...

1274
00:50:20,457 --> 00:50:21,526
I was a rifleman too.

1275
00:50:21,527 --> 00:50:24,496
The place I was in Iraq was...

1276
00:50:24,497 --> 00:50:27,596
Erbil where the peacekeeping forces were.

1277
00:50:27,597 --> 00:50:29,227
It was a pretty safe area.

1278
00:50:29,567 --> 00:50:33,396
But I also went to places like Tikrit and Baghdad...

1279
00:50:33,397 --> 00:50:35,636
where the US bases were.

1280
00:50:35,637 --> 00:50:37,236
As a translator.

1281
00:50:37,237 --> 00:50:38,906
You must be really fluent in English.

1282
00:50:38,907 --> 00:50:40,876
When you're there,

1283
00:50:40,877 --> 00:50:43,406
once a sandstorm occurs, the plane can't take off.

1284
00:50:43,407 --> 00:50:44,747
For a week or two.

1285
00:50:45,747 --> 00:50:47,146
- You get isolated.
- I was isolated.

1286
00:50:47,147 --> 00:50:49,147
When I'm isolated...

1287
00:50:49,787 --> 00:50:51,157
There were...

1288
00:50:51,617 --> 00:50:55,256
Japanese or Australians...

1289
00:50:55,257 --> 00:50:56,326
- From other countries.
- There were soldiers...

1290
00:50:56,327 --> 00:50:57,396
from other countries.

1291
00:50:57,397 --> 00:51:00,696
We played soccer or basketball together and ate together.

1292
00:51:00,697 --> 00:51:04,767
We exchanged guns to check them out.

1293
00:51:05,837 --> 00:51:07,967
We became very close.

1294
00:51:09,037 --> 00:51:11,676
You built a lot of good memories.

1295
00:51:11,677 --> 00:51:15,247
(The time when the 23-year-old Suk Ku learned the broader world)

1296
00:51:15,807 --> 00:51:17,817
I still keep in touch with the ones I was deployed with.

1297
00:51:18,147 --> 00:51:21,516
I think it might be better...

1298
00:51:21,517 --> 00:51:23,586
to go abroad and hang out...

1299
00:51:23,587 --> 00:51:24,916
with soldiers from all around the world.

1300
00:51:24,917 --> 00:51:26,816
- It was romantic.
- Right.

1301
00:51:26,817 --> 00:51:28,287
It was a new experience.

1302
00:51:29,157 --> 00:51:30,256
And I got paid a lot too.

1303
00:51:30,257 --> 00:51:31,326
(Frankly speaking)

1304
00:51:31,327 --> 00:51:32,857
The hazard pay is very high.

1305
00:51:33,657 --> 00:51:36,427
So when I returned from Iraq,

1306
00:51:36,867 --> 00:51:39,167
I made just over 12,000 dollars.

1307
00:51:39,837 --> 00:51:42,467
That's how I was able to go to Vancouver to learn acting.

1308
00:51:42,837 --> 00:51:44,606
I paid for a plane ticket to Vancouver with it.

1309
00:51:44,607 --> 00:51:45,906
It wasn't out of your father's pocket?

1310
00:51:45,907 --> 00:51:47,176
- No.
- Out of your own pocket.

1311
00:51:47,177 --> 00:51:49,507
I paid for my own acting lessons.

1312
00:51:50,377 --> 00:51:52,547
It'll work out if you try.

1313
00:51:52,877 --> 00:51:54,446
You become fearless.

1314
00:51:54,447 --> 00:51:55,517
(It became a foundation for his dream.)

1315
00:51:56,517 --> 00:51:59,887
The only celebrities in Korea who were deployed are...

1316
00:52:01,387 --> 00:52:03,486
Nam Jin and...

1317
00:52:03,487 --> 00:52:04,496
Yes.

1318
00:52:04,497 --> 00:52:06,497
him. Just the two of them.

1319
00:52:06,957 --> 00:52:08,896
And they both appeared in our show.

1320
00:52:08,897 --> 00:52:09,927
You're right.

1321
00:52:10,697 --> 00:52:13,336
But then Nam Jin actually entered enemy's territory.

1322
00:52:13,337 --> 00:52:15,266
- Yes.
- I didn't do that.

1323
00:52:15,267 --> 00:52:16,467
He's on another level.

1324
00:52:17,037 --> 00:52:20,447
(Suk Ku is just as praiseworthy.)

1325
00:52:21,507 --> 00:52:23,776
It's time to meet the audience.

1326
00:52:23,777 --> 00:52:25,546
Okay. Are you going alone?

1327
00:52:25,547 --> 00:52:26,646
You should join us.

1328
00:52:26,647 --> 00:52:27,686
I won't be off until 10pm.

1329
00:52:27,687 --> 00:52:29,916
- If there's a break in between.
- If I get a break.

1330
00:52:29,917 --> 00:52:31,017
Talk to you later, Suk Ku.

1331
00:52:31,317 --> 00:52:33,457
- Hey. Good luck.
- Thank you.

1332
00:52:34,127 --> 00:52:35,826
(While Seo Jin's paying)

1333
00:52:35,827 --> 00:52:36,887
Thank you.

1334
00:52:37,397 --> 00:52:39,127
- Right.
- I actually...

1335
00:52:39,757 --> 00:52:41,396
mentioned bibimbap.

1336
00:52:41,397 --> 00:52:43,596
- You like Korean food.
- I didn't really want bibimbap.

1337
00:52:43,597 --> 00:52:45,037
(The two picked different menus.)

1338
00:52:45,437 --> 00:52:47,136
Seo Jin said he was okay with Japanese.

1339
00:52:47,137 --> 00:52:49,366
Hey. Even if Seo Jin said that,

1340
00:52:49,367 --> 00:52:51,376
you should've said what you wanted to eat.

1341
00:52:51,377 --> 00:52:53,606
You were tough on me.

1342
00:52:53,607 --> 00:52:55,306
Are you tough on weak but weak on tough?

1343
00:52:55,307 --> 00:52:57,006
- Come on.
- That's not it.

1344
00:52:57,007 --> 00:52:59,216
After today,

1345
00:52:59,217 --> 00:53:01,087
I think I get along with Seo Jin better.

1346
00:53:02,417 --> 00:53:03,957
I'm saying this because I like him.

1347
00:53:04,357 --> 00:53:08,157
(A bolt from the blue)

1348
00:53:08,457 --> 00:53:09,586
Sorry for going back on my word.

1349
00:53:09,587 --> 00:53:10,656
No.

1350
00:53:10,657 --> 00:53:13,226
Even if you like him, go tough on him at least once.

1351
00:53:13,227 --> 00:53:14,526
Then...

1352
00:53:14,527 --> 00:53:17,567
While Seo Jin's off guard,

1353
00:53:17,837 --> 00:53:20,536
you should grab him by the collar out of nowhere.

1354
00:53:20,537 --> 00:53:23,066
- That's...
- Will you please do it?

1355
00:53:23,067 --> 00:53:24,336
- But...
- You...

1356
00:53:24,337 --> 00:53:25,676
What do I do after that?

1357
00:53:25,677 --> 00:53:28,046
Say, "You've been kidnapped."

1358
00:53:28,047 --> 00:53:29,576
But that's so random.

1359
00:53:29,577 --> 00:53:31,277
That's what variety shows are about.

1360
00:53:32,647 --> 00:53:33,676
It doesn't matter.

1361
00:53:33,677 --> 00:53:35,146
(How can I do that to Seo Jin?)

1362
00:53:35,147 --> 00:53:36,417
That's what you do.

1363
00:53:37,317 --> 00:53:38,356
Okay. I'll try.

1364
00:53:38,357 --> 00:53:39,716
Why are you scared?

1365
00:53:39,717 --> 00:53:40,856
We have to go.

1366
00:53:40,857 --> 00:53:42,387
- Okay. Let's go.
- We have to go.

1367
00:53:42,827 --> 00:53:45,057
Let's do this.

1368
00:53:46,327 --> 00:53:49,567
(1:10pm, "The Blue Road" screening)

1369
00:53:49,597 --> 00:53:51,337
Are you only greeting the audience?

1370
00:53:51,767 --> 00:53:53,196
Greet the audience and watch it.

1371
00:53:53,197 --> 00:53:55,166
Greeting... You're watching the movie too?

1372
00:53:55,167 --> 00:53:56,806
- Yes.
- And then talk to the audience?

1373
00:53:56,807 --> 00:53:58,036
- It looks like it.
- Okay.

1374
00:53:58,037 --> 00:53:59,137
(Greeting the audience after watching "The Blue Road")

1375
00:53:59,337 --> 00:54:00,777
Will there be other actors?

1376
00:54:01,647 --> 00:54:03,776
Shin Rock from earlier.

1377
00:54:03,777 --> 00:54:04,876
(Kim Shin Rock)

1378
00:54:04,877 --> 00:54:06,177
Eita Nagayama.

1379
00:54:06,477 --> 00:54:07,586
And the director.

1380
00:54:07,587 --> 00:54:08,587
(The actors of "The Blue Road")

1381
00:54:09,617 --> 00:54:11,616
(Reading Kwang Kyu's face)

1382
00:54:11,617 --> 00:54:13,117
Hold my bag.

1383
00:54:13,257 --> 00:54:16,856
- Kwang Kyu told me...
- Okay.

1384
00:54:16,857 --> 00:54:18,096
(Whispering)

1385
00:54:18,097 --> 00:54:19,457
to grab you by the collar...

1386
00:54:19,597 --> 00:54:21,797
out of nowhere...

1387
00:54:22,127 --> 00:54:24,696
- and say, "You've been kidnapped."
- What?

1388
00:54:24,697 --> 00:54:27,196
He told me to say, "You've been kidnapped."

1389
00:54:27,197 --> 00:54:28,807
(Glancing)

1390
00:54:29,437 --> 00:54:31,877
(What are they talking about?)

1391
00:54:31,907 --> 00:54:34,106
(Bitter)

1392
00:54:34,107 --> 00:54:36,477
He told me to say, "You've been kidnapped."

1393
00:54:36,777 --> 00:54:37,816
So...

1394
00:54:37,817 --> 00:54:39,777
Don't. That's lame.

1395
00:54:40,517 --> 00:54:41,687
- Right?
- Yes.

1396
00:54:42,717 --> 00:54:44,087
If I do it,

1397
00:54:44,657 --> 00:54:47,427
why don't you get all serious...

1398
00:54:47,827 --> 00:54:49,427
and startle Kwang Kyu?

1399
00:54:52,297 --> 00:54:53,427
No.

1400
00:54:54,297 --> 00:54:55,727
No. That's lame.

1401
00:54:55,867 --> 00:54:57,366
- Right?
- That's lame.

1402
00:54:57,367 --> 00:54:58,597
(Suk Ku betrays Kwang Kyu.)

1403
00:54:59,137 --> 00:55:00,397
(Reading the room)

1404
00:55:01,837 --> 00:55:03,037
What is this tension in the air?

1405
00:55:04,607 --> 00:55:06,576
You're not talking behind my back, are you?

1406
00:55:06,577 --> 00:55:07,747
(Feeling isolated)

1407
00:55:08,007 --> 00:55:10,547
I'd talk in front of you, not behind your back.

1408
00:55:11,947 --> 00:55:14,246
- Am I wrong?
- Watch your mouth...

1409
00:55:14,247 --> 00:55:16,547
in front of Suk Ku.

1410
00:55:17,557 --> 00:55:18,986
Be a good example.

1411
00:55:18,987 --> 00:55:20,117
See?

1412
00:55:20,587 --> 00:55:23,157
(Suk Ku, do it now!)

1413
00:55:23,187 --> 00:55:24,227
See?

1414
00:55:25,227 --> 00:55:30,167
(Here's what Kwang Kyu wanted.)

1415
00:55:30,667 --> 00:55:31,736
(Vicarious satisfaction)

1416
00:55:31,737 --> 00:55:32,796
Happy now?

1417
00:55:32,797 --> 00:55:34,866
(Laughing)

1418
00:55:34,867 --> 00:55:36,137
He's so happy.

1419
00:55:37,137 --> 00:55:38,137
That's funny.

1420
00:55:38,577 --> 00:55:39,676
Yes.

1421
00:55:39,677 --> 00:55:41,177
I like that.

1422
00:55:43,477 --> 00:55:45,047
Good job.

1423
00:55:45,677 --> 00:55:48,287
Do that every time he grabs me by the collar.

1424
00:55:48,887 --> 00:55:49,887
Do that every time.

1425
00:55:49,888 --> 00:55:51,887
- What was that?
- You seem worried.

1426
00:55:53,317 --> 00:55:55,127
- No.
- What?

1427
00:55:55,887 --> 00:55:57,427
See?

1428
00:55:59,197 --> 00:56:03,427
(No one ever looks so happy grabbing someone by the collar.)

1429
00:56:06,437 --> 00:56:07,607
I did my best.

1430
00:56:07,937 --> 00:56:09,107
Good job.

1431
00:56:10,407 --> 00:56:12,037
I wish you grabbed it stronger.

1432
00:56:13,807 --> 00:56:16,577
(Kwang Kyu's sad he didn't grab it stronger.)

1433
00:56:17,077 --> 00:56:20,576
I hope you enjoy watching the series.

1434
00:56:20,577 --> 00:56:21,617
Of course.

1435
00:56:21,787 --> 00:56:23,817
- Are we all watching it together?
- We are.

1436
00:56:24,017 --> 00:56:26,656
Don't hesitate to criticize it after watching.

1437
00:56:26,657 --> 00:56:28,127
Oh, I'm sure it's good.

1438
00:56:29,357 --> 00:56:31,026
- I hope you enjoy watching.
- What?

1439
00:56:31,027 --> 00:56:33,026
- I hope you enjoy watching.
- I bet it's good.

1440
00:56:33,027 --> 00:56:34,167
After watching...

1441
00:56:34,497 --> 00:56:36,427
Out of eight episodes,

1442
00:56:36,497 --> 00:56:38,436
only three episodes will play.

1443
00:56:38,437 --> 00:56:42,036
It stops after the introduction.

1444
00:56:42,037 --> 00:56:45,376
(Getting nervous before the premiere)

1445
00:56:45,377 --> 00:56:48,676
(It's starting to look obvious that he's nervous.)

1446
00:56:48,677 --> 00:56:50,847
- I'm getting nervous.
- What for?

1447
00:56:50,977 --> 00:56:54,487
To meet the audience again after a long time...

1448
00:56:57,047 --> 00:57:01,557
(Tension makes My Star quiet.)

1449
00:57:01,587 --> 00:57:03,456
Kwang Kyu, help Suk Ku relax.

1450
00:57:03,457 --> 00:57:04,996
- Should I sing or something?
- Yes.

1451
00:57:04,997 --> 00:57:06,056
Yes!

1452
00:57:06,057 --> 00:57:07,057
(Yes!)

1453
00:57:07,058 --> 00:57:08,097
Yes.

1454
00:57:08,467 --> 00:57:10,096
- Hey.
- Please.

1455
00:57:10,097 --> 00:57:11,737
(Please sing a song.)

1456
00:57:11,797 --> 00:57:14,607
- We do anything My Star asks.
- Yes.

1457
00:57:15,067 --> 00:57:16,467
- Sing.
- Yes.

1458
00:57:16,837 --> 00:57:18,637
Just until we pass this tunnel.

1459
00:57:18,707 --> 00:57:19,876
- What? Now?
- Yes.

1460
00:57:19,877 --> 00:57:21,506
I thought you were telling me to sing on stage.

1461
00:57:21,507 --> 00:57:22,606
- On stage?
- On stage?

1462
00:57:22,607 --> 00:57:24,777
Why would you do that? It's not even your movie.

1463
00:57:24,817 --> 00:57:26,047
You want to sing on stage?

1464
00:57:26,317 --> 00:57:27,917
No, to break the ice.

1465
00:57:27,987 --> 00:57:30,217
I thought you were telling me to sing to break the ice.

1466
00:57:31,557 --> 00:57:32,757
Gosh.

1467
00:57:33,287 --> 00:57:34,427
Hello.

1468
00:57:34,487 --> 00:57:35,656
He's Son Suk Ku.

1469
00:57:35,657 --> 00:57:37,387
(Promoting Son Suk Ku since it's awkward)

1470
00:57:38,257 --> 00:57:39,696
Hello.

1471
00:57:39,697 --> 00:57:41,097
Why am I getting so nervous?

1472
00:57:41,397 --> 00:57:42,766
Do you want to sit here?

1473
00:57:42,767 --> 00:57:44,497
- Why is it so hot?
- Right?

1474
00:57:44,567 --> 00:57:45,697
It's hot.

1475
00:57:46,037 --> 00:57:47,196
I didn't have...

1476
00:57:47,197 --> 00:57:48,507
time to prepare matching T-shirts.

1477
00:57:48,807 --> 00:57:50,707
- Let's put this on.
- What's that?

1478
00:57:53,007 --> 00:57:54,107
What does it say?

1479
00:57:54,407 --> 00:57:55,476
That's the poster.

1480
00:57:55,477 --> 00:57:56,606
- "The Blue Road" poster?
- Yes.

1481
00:57:56,607 --> 00:57:58,677
(My Star prepared the poster sticker of "The Blue Road.")

1482
00:57:58,817 --> 00:57:59,946
Why don't you put it on your forehead?

1483
00:57:59,947 --> 00:58:01,087
- What?
- Put it on your forehead.

1484
00:58:01,347 --> 00:58:03,417
This is when you grab him by the collar.

1485
00:58:03,747 --> 00:58:04,786
Gosh.

1486
00:58:04,787 --> 00:58:06,217
(Smiling)

1487
00:58:06,287 --> 00:58:07,486
- You...
- Put it on your forehead.

1488
00:58:07,487 --> 00:58:08,586
Put it on anywhere you want.

1489
00:58:08,587 --> 00:58:10,287
- On the forehead.
- On the forehead?

1490
00:58:10,627 --> 00:58:12,097
Fine. Do it.

1491
00:58:12,697 --> 00:58:13,856
- Do it.
- Just do it.

1492
00:58:13,857 --> 00:58:15,026
Let me do it.

1493
00:58:15,027 --> 00:58:16,326
- Or do it on my cheek.
- You want it on his forehead?

1494
00:58:16,327 --> 00:58:17,997
- How dare you!
- Good job.

1495
00:58:18,397 --> 00:58:20,137
- Put it on him.
- See?

1496
00:58:20,497 --> 00:58:22,367
- You do it.
- Give me that.

1497
00:58:22,907 --> 00:58:23,966
Hey.

1498
00:58:23,967 --> 00:58:25,177
- I know you like it.
- Hey.

1499
00:58:25,907 --> 00:58:27,176
(Absurd)

1500
00:58:27,177 --> 00:58:28,276
Are you out of your mind?

1501
00:58:28,277 --> 00:58:29,947
(Absurd)

1502
00:58:30,877 --> 00:58:32,116
(As long as it makes My Star laugh)

1503
00:58:32,117 --> 00:58:33,577
- It's funny, though.
- Hey.

1504
00:58:34,047 --> 00:58:36,587
This is not even ridiculous.

1505
00:58:37,617 --> 00:58:38,656
There.

1506
00:58:38,657 --> 00:58:39,816
(He's willing to give up his forehead.)

1507
00:58:39,817 --> 00:58:40,926
Let's take a picture.

1508
00:58:40,927 --> 00:58:42,627
(He's willing to give up his forehead.)

1509
00:58:43,687 --> 00:58:44,797
Thank you.

1510
00:58:45,227 --> 00:58:46,427
It's perfect.

1511
00:58:46,457 --> 00:58:48,227
I'm a walking billboard.

1512
00:58:49,697 --> 00:58:50,867
Hello.

1513
00:58:52,467 --> 00:58:54,237
I really enjoyed watching "Uncle Vanya."

1514
00:58:54,437 --> 00:58:55,866
- Have you seen it?
- Of course.

1515
00:58:55,867 --> 00:58:56,906
Really? You came to see it?

1516
00:58:56,907 --> 00:58:58,006
- What? Yes.
- You came to see it?

1517
00:58:58,007 --> 00:59:00,177
Really? I see.

1518
00:59:00,207 --> 00:59:02,046
- Nice to meet you.
- Thank you for watching.

1519
00:59:02,047 --> 00:59:04,247
- Have a seat.
- Have a seat.

1520
00:59:04,377 --> 00:59:05,976
- Please have a seat.
- Have a seat.

1521
00:59:05,977 --> 00:59:07,146
(A guest that just a simple hello isn't enough)

1522
00:59:07,147 --> 00:59:08,346
Have you met her before?

1523
00:59:08,347 --> 00:59:09,986
- No.
- No, right?

1524
00:59:09,987 --> 00:59:12,057
- I've seen you on TV.
- You put it on your forehead.

1525
00:59:12,117 --> 00:59:13,286
He volunteered to do it.

1526
00:59:13,287 --> 00:59:15,087
- For the movie.
- Yes.

1527
00:59:15,787 --> 00:59:16,827
That's...

1528
00:59:17,727 --> 00:59:19,796
I'm nervous about the premiere.

1529
00:59:19,797 --> 00:59:20,926
Me too.

1530
00:59:20,927 --> 00:59:22,796
- Don't be.
- I haven't seen it.

1531
00:59:22,797 --> 00:59:24,296
I'm sure it's good.

1532
00:59:24,297 --> 00:59:25,937
(With all of you starring)

1533
00:59:26,597 --> 00:59:28,566
"The Blue Road," let's start moving.

1534
00:59:28,567 --> 00:59:29,607
Let's get going.

1535
00:59:30,267 --> 00:59:31,276
(Finally to the theater)

1536
00:59:31,277 --> 00:59:32,306
Let's go.

1537
00:59:32,307 --> 00:59:33,307
(Finally to the theater)

1538
00:59:33,677 --> 00:59:35,407
- So nervous, Director.
- Me?

1539
00:59:35,447 --> 00:59:36,547
No, me.

1540
00:59:37,477 --> 00:59:38,947
You've seen it.

1541
00:59:39,117 --> 00:59:40,146
I'm nervous too.

1542
00:59:40,147 --> 00:59:41,417
This is my first time watching it with the audience.

1543
00:59:43,587 --> 00:59:46,056
(My Star is very nervous before the premiere.)

1544
00:59:46,057 --> 00:59:48,686
I hope my secretaries enjoy it too.

1545
00:59:48,687 --> 00:59:49,727
I know.

1546
00:59:50,457 --> 00:59:54,697
(My Star is looking forward to the secretaries' review.)

1547
00:59:55,627 --> 00:59:56,766
(Actor Eita Nagayama)

1548
00:59:56,767 --> 00:59:57,897
- Nervous?
- Yes.

1549
00:59:58,667 --> 00:59:59,866
Nervous.

1550
00:59:59,867 --> 01:00:01,407
- Nervous.
- Nervous.

1551
01:00:01,537 --> 01:00:03,036
I'm nervous.

1552
01:00:03,037 --> 01:00:04,237
Very much.

1553
01:00:04,477 --> 01:00:05,776
This is crazy.

1554
01:00:05,777 --> 01:00:07,676
(This is crazy.)

1555
01:00:07,677 --> 01:00:08,777
What?

1556
01:00:08,847 --> 01:00:10,876
I haven't been this nervous.

1557
01:00:10,877 --> 01:00:12,216
- Really?
- Yes.

1558
01:00:12,217 --> 01:00:13,747
(I haven't been this nervous.)

1559
01:00:14,347 --> 01:00:18,457
(Even the veteran actor gets nervous about the special screening.)

1560
01:00:20,717 --> 01:00:25,557
(Don't worry. I got your back.)

1561
01:00:28,367 --> 01:00:31,296
(Entering the theater nervously)

1562
01:00:31,297 --> 01:00:32,566
Are we watching the movie first?

1563
01:00:32,567 --> 01:00:33,967
- The movie first?
- Yes, after the movie.

1564
01:00:34,967 --> 01:00:36,437
Without saying hello first?

1565
01:00:36,507 --> 01:00:38,436
I guess they're going to watch it first.

1566
01:00:38,437 --> 01:00:39,607
- Really?
- Yes.

1567
01:00:39,837 --> 01:00:42,346
(Checking their seats)

1568
01:00:42,347 --> 01:00:43,477
What's that?

1569
01:00:44,817 --> 01:00:45,817
Gosh.

1570
01:00:45,818 --> 01:00:47,346
(My Star sits next to his fellow actors.)

1571
01:00:47,347 --> 01:00:49,017
- Suk Ku.
- Enjoy watching.

1572
01:00:49,687 --> 01:00:51,157
- You are so handsome.
- Thank you.

1573
01:00:51,787 --> 01:00:54,256
My parents are here somewhere.

1574
01:00:54,257 --> 01:00:55,357
Hello.

1575
01:00:56,757 --> 01:00:58,496
My parents are here.

1576
01:00:58,497 --> 01:00:59,497
(Where are they?)

1577
01:00:59,997 --> 01:01:01,366
- Hello.
- Hello.

1578
01:01:01,367 --> 01:01:04,467
(Hello.)

1579
01:01:05,467 --> 01:01:07,436
(Sitting next to the audience)

1580
01:01:07,437 --> 01:01:08,937
Sorry about the shoot.

1581
01:01:09,867 --> 01:01:11,077
How will it look?

1582
01:01:11,977 --> 01:01:13,637
(Glancing)

1583
01:01:14,377 --> 01:01:15,776
- Are you here alone?
- Yes.

1584
01:01:15,777 --> 01:01:16,877
- What?
- Yes.

1585
01:01:16,947 --> 01:01:18,047
To see Son Suk Ku?

1586
01:01:18,177 --> 01:01:19,277
No?

1587
01:01:19,717 --> 01:01:21,717
- To see all actors.
- I see.

1588
01:01:23,087 --> 01:01:24,886
- Do you live in Busan?
- No.

1589
01:01:24,887 --> 01:01:26,056
- Seoul.
- Where? From Seoul?

1590
01:01:26,057 --> 01:01:27,157
Really?

1591
01:01:27,787 --> 01:01:29,086
What? Is it starting already?

1592
01:01:29,087 --> 01:01:30,257
(The blackout announces the start of the movie.)

1593
01:01:31,357 --> 01:01:32,557
Thank you for the movie.

1594
01:01:34,767 --> 01:01:35,826
Here it comes.

1595
01:01:35,827 --> 01:01:40,467
(The premiere of "The Blue Road")

1596
01:01:53,647 --> 01:01:56,086
(A twisted body and a mysterious message)

1597
01:01:56,087 --> 01:01:58,556
(It's a story about two detectives...)

1598
01:01:58,557 --> 01:02:01,326
(who are after a series of brutal murders...)

1599
01:02:01,327 --> 01:02:04,087
(that go beyond the border.)

1600
01:02:06,727 --> 01:02:10,396
(Son Suk Ku as a detective from Seoul Police Station)

1601
01:02:10,397 --> 01:02:14,196
(Eita Nagayama as a detective from Tokyo Police Station)

1602
01:02:14,197 --> 01:02:17,976
(Tension between two opposite detectives...)

1603
01:02:17,977 --> 01:02:21,446
(and new buddy chemistry)

1604
01:02:21,447 --> 01:02:24,977
(Han Jun Hee's hardboiled crime thriller)

1605
01:02:35,857 --> 01:02:37,487
It has a solid storyline.

1606
01:02:38,927 --> 01:02:42,396
Each character is strong,

1607
01:02:42,397 --> 01:02:43,397
yet unique.

1608
01:02:43,627 --> 01:02:45,697
Suk Ku's role is...

1609
01:02:45,797 --> 01:02:48,037
somewhat stiff.

1610
01:02:48,237 --> 01:02:49,707
He doesn't show much emotion.

1611
01:02:49,767 --> 01:02:52,107
Yet, Eita...

1612
01:02:52,277 --> 01:02:55,046
His acting is...

1613
01:02:55,047 --> 01:02:56,706
very flexible.

1614
01:02:56,707 --> 01:02:58,716
That formed harmony.

1615
01:02:58,717 --> 01:02:59,847
(That formed harmony between them.)

1616
01:02:59,977 --> 01:03:01,447
It takes place in 2002.

1617
01:03:02,187 --> 01:03:03,786
So...

1618
01:03:03,787 --> 01:03:05,156
I noticed...

1619
01:03:05,157 --> 01:03:07,457
it was given an old color.

1620
01:03:07,887 --> 01:03:09,787
Like an old film.

1621
01:03:10,557 --> 01:03:11,656
That's how it was made.

1622
01:03:11,657 --> 01:03:13,727
Details like that.

1623
01:03:13,827 --> 01:03:15,926
The film design and costumes were intended...

1624
01:03:15,927 --> 01:03:18,737
to look old-fashioned on purpose.

1625
01:03:19,497 --> 01:03:21,337
I could tell that they focused on that.

1626
01:03:24,037 --> 01:03:26,137
What was the most memorable scene?

1627
01:03:28,047 --> 01:03:29,146
The tiger?

1628
01:03:29,147 --> 01:03:30,607
(The tiger?)

1629
01:03:31,877 --> 01:03:33,577
The tiger. What?

1630
01:03:33,817 --> 01:03:35,616
There was a tiger in the movie.

1631
01:03:35,617 --> 01:03:37,316
(It might be a very important clue.)

1632
01:03:37,317 --> 01:03:40,216
Let's bring the director and three actors...

1633
01:03:40,217 --> 01:03:41,987
to the stage.

1634
01:03:42,327 --> 01:03:44,087
Please greet them with a big round of applause.

1635
01:03:44,387 --> 01:03:47,097
Director Han Jun Hee and Son Suk Ku.

1636
01:03:47,397 --> 01:03:50,227
Eita Nagayama and Kim Shin Rock.

1637
01:03:51,697 --> 01:03:53,666
Did you enjoy watching?

1638
01:03:53,667 --> 01:03:54,837
- Yes.
- Is this on?

1639
01:03:55,367 --> 01:03:56,606
What did you think?

1640
01:03:56,607 --> 01:03:58,007
- It was fun.
- It was good.

1641
01:03:58,277 --> 01:03:59,907
(Laughing)

1642
01:04:00,007 --> 01:04:02,376
The first scene...

1643
01:04:02,377 --> 01:04:05,177
we filmed was...

1644
01:04:05,577 --> 01:04:06,816
the investigation room scene in Tokyo.

1645
01:04:06,817 --> 01:04:08,487
The conversation in the investigation room...

1646
01:04:08,587 --> 01:04:10,446
was our first shoot...

1647
01:04:10,447 --> 01:04:11,787
on the first day.

1648
01:04:11,887 --> 01:04:13,356
I instantly...

1649
01:04:13,357 --> 01:04:15,426
got a feeling...

1650
01:04:15,427 --> 01:04:17,657
that this guy...

1651
01:04:17,827 --> 01:04:20,097
really knew how to act.

1652
01:04:20,327 --> 01:04:21,566
So...

1653
01:04:21,567 --> 01:04:23,127
he was...

1654
01:04:23,697 --> 01:04:26,767
the best actor I've ever worked with so far.

1655
01:04:27,797 --> 01:04:29,807
I mean it.

1656
01:04:30,037 --> 01:04:32,837
I've said this to the director again and again.

1657
01:04:33,677 --> 01:04:36,747
It was so fun to work with him.

1658
01:04:37,707 --> 01:04:38,917
Thank you.

1659
01:04:39,977 --> 01:04:41,417
Me too.

1660
01:04:43,147 --> 01:04:46,957
I wouldn't mind...

1661
01:04:47,717 --> 01:04:51,556
even if this becomes the last film in my life.

1662
01:04:51,557 --> 01:04:53,956
That's how much I was immersed in this with Suk Ku.

1663
01:04:53,957 --> 01:04:56,026
(That's how much I was immersed in this with Suk Ku.)

1664
01:04:56,027 --> 01:05:00,167
(Thank you, Eita.)

1665
01:05:03,007 --> 01:05:04,367
Eita...

1666
01:05:04,507 --> 01:05:06,507
looks better on screen.

1667
01:05:08,247 --> 01:05:10,047
Because his acting is so good,

1668
01:05:10,077 --> 01:05:11,517
he stands out on screen.

1669
01:05:12,717 --> 01:05:14,377
- Right.
- He stands out on screen.

1670
01:05:18,087 --> 01:05:19,457
He has a really nice voice.

1671
01:05:19,517 --> 01:05:20,757
Listen to him.

1672
01:05:21,087 --> 01:05:22,157
Right?

1673
01:05:22,687 --> 01:05:24,056
Amazing.

1674
01:05:24,057 --> 01:05:26,497
(Amazing)

1675
01:05:26,857 --> 01:05:28,696
If you have any questions, raise your hand,

1676
01:05:28,697 --> 01:05:30,267
and we'll bring you the mic.

1677
01:05:30,867 --> 01:05:33,436
The lines that weren't in your language...

1678
01:05:33,437 --> 01:05:36,507
Detective Kim Seok...

1679
01:05:36,567 --> 01:05:39,776
For what reason did you choose these three actors?

1680
01:05:39,777 --> 01:05:41,076
Thanks for the streaming service.

1681
01:05:41,077 --> 01:05:42,406
(Thank you for the streaming service.)

1682
01:05:42,407 --> 01:05:44,547
If it wouldn't spoil the movie...

1683
01:05:44,577 --> 01:05:46,747
It will spoil the movie.

1684
01:05:47,717 --> 01:05:49,947
We only have time for one last question.

1685
01:05:50,347 --> 01:05:52,687
We have special managers here.

1686
01:05:52,957 --> 01:05:55,356
If you have any questions,

1687
01:05:55,357 --> 01:05:58,397
we'll let you take the last question.

1688
01:05:58,827 --> 01:06:00,826
- Can someone get him the mic?
- Oh, no.

1689
01:06:00,827 --> 01:06:01,967
(It's my secretaries.)

1690
01:06:02,767 --> 01:06:07,237
(Seo Jin is given a mic.)

1691
01:06:08,137 --> 01:06:09,467
Hello.

1692
01:06:10,637 --> 01:06:13,507
I'm Son Suk Ku's manager for today. I'm Lee Seo Jin.

1693
01:06:15,547 --> 01:06:19,677
(They're my secretaries.)

1694
01:06:21,617 --> 01:06:24,017
I got the feeling that it has a solid storyline.

1695
01:06:24,087 --> 01:06:27,156
Each character is unique,

1696
01:06:27,157 --> 01:06:29,727
yet they form nice harmony.

1697
01:06:30,727 --> 01:06:33,356
(Relieved)

1698
01:06:33,357 --> 01:06:36,067
I have a question for the director.

1699
01:06:38,797 --> 01:06:40,997
(A question for the director after his sharp review)

1700
01:06:41,407 --> 01:06:45,137
(My Star also gets nervous.)

1701
01:06:45,837 --> 01:06:49,446
(What's Seo Jin's question?)

1702
01:06:49,447 --> 01:06:50,877
We have...

1703
01:06:51,007 --> 01:06:53,277
- Actor Kim Kwang Kyu here.
- Okay.

1704
01:06:53,817 --> 01:06:57,987
Would you be willing to cast Kim Kwang Kyu in your next work?

1705
01:06:58,787 --> 01:07:00,516
Would you be willing to cast...

1706
01:07:00,517 --> 01:07:02,887
Kim Kwang Kyu in your next work?

1707
01:07:04,087 --> 01:07:06,597
(I'm counting on you.)

1708
01:07:09,867 --> 01:07:12,437
I'm a big fan of Kwang Kyu.

1709
01:07:12,497 --> 01:07:15,737
When writing scripts,

1710
01:07:16,007 --> 01:07:17,607
I haven't always had you in mind,

1711
01:07:17,837 --> 01:07:20,577
but I'll try to write a role that suits you in my next project.

1712
01:07:20,707 --> 01:07:22,247
I haven't always had you in mind,

1713
01:07:22,447 --> 01:07:25,417
but I'll try to write a role that suits you...

1714
01:07:25,617 --> 01:07:27,246
in my next project.

1715
01:07:27,247 --> 01:07:28,416
Thank you.

1716
01:07:28,417 --> 01:07:30,316
Good luck to "The Blue Road."

1717
01:07:30,317 --> 01:07:31,456
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1718
01:07:31,457 --> 01:07:34,057
My parting words to you, Director, are, "What does your father do?"

1719
01:07:34,257 --> 01:07:35,326
Thank you.

1720
01:07:35,327 --> 01:07:36,987
(Proud of himself for squeezing in a catchphrase)

1721
01:07:37,357 --> 01:07:38,357
(Feeling bad)

1722
01:07:38,357 --> 01:07:39,357
Thank you.

1723
01:07:40,757 --> 01:07:42,467
- All right.
- The director...

1724
01:07:42,667 --> 01:07:43,897
isn't good at telling white lies.

1725
01:07:46,037 --> 01:07:47,337
That wishy-washy answer.

1726
01:07:47,867 --> 01:07:49,407
It's bugging me.

1727
01:07:51,807 --> 01:07:53,007
I don't want it to end.

1728
01:07:53,107 --> 01:07:55,277
If only we could do this for another hour.

1729
01:07:55,547 --> 01:07:58,176
Right? I'd love to ask everyone...

1730
01:07:58,177 --> 01:08:00,347
one-on-one, "How was it?"

1731
01:08:00,817 --> 01:08:03,617
"What would you give it out of ten?" I'd like to ask.

1732
01:08:04,317 --> 01:08:06,086
Anyway, I'll see you again.

1733
01:08:06,087 --> 01:08:08,627
(Reluctantly wrapping up the Q and A for "The Blue Road")

1734
01:08:08,727 --> 01:08:09,757
Thank you.

1735
01:08:11,157 --> 01:08:12,756
(Liberated from his schedule)

1736
01:08:12,757 --> 01:08:13,826
Great work.

1737
01:08:13,827 --> 01:08:16,096
Thank you.

1738
01:08:16,097 --> 01:08:17,227
(Thank you.)

1739
01:08:17,997 --> 01:08:19,967
(Suk Ku, accept our gifts!)

1740
01:08:20,697 --> 01:08:22,337
- Thank you.
- Oh, my gosh.

1741
01:08:22,807 --> 01:08:23,837
Thank you.

1742
01:08:24,467 --> 01:08:25,977
(Asking for an autograph)

1743
01:08:26,807 --> 01:08:28,006
(My Star knows how to treat the fans right.)

1744
01:08:28,007 --> 01:08:29,746
Thank you. Bye.

1745
01:08:29,747 --> 01:08:30,807
(My Star knows how to treat the fans right.)

1746
01:08:31,307 --> 01:08:32,947
- We...
- Where are we going?

1747
01:08:33,377 --> 01:08:34,746
Aren't we grabbing food?

1748
01:08:34,747 --> 01:08:36,017
- No.
- Already?

1749
01:08:36,187 --> 01:08:38,217
Isn't it too early for food?

1750
01:08:38,557 --> 01:08:40,187
Is that so? Is there something you want to do?

1751
01:08:40,457 --> 01:08:42,627
Now that I finally feel relaxed...

1752
01:08:43,857 --> 01:08:45,497
- A match.
- What?

1753
01:08:45,797 --> 01:08:47,326
- Basketball.
- Basketball?

1754
01:08:47,327 --> 01:08:48,327
Yes.

1755
01:08:48,884 --> 01:08:50,134
(My Star's liberation notes after his schedule)

1756
01:08:50,166 --> 01:08:52,266
Are you ready?

1757
01:08:52,736 --> 01:08:53,766
So?

1758
01:08:54,336 --> 01:08:55,835
- Shall we bet?
- Yes.

1759
01:08:55,836 --> 01:08:56,836
What kind of bet?

1760
01:08:56,837 --> 01:08:58,375
We each get three balls.

1761
01:08:58,376 --> 01:08:59,405
(A showdown between basketball players)

1762
01:08:59,406 --> 01:09:00,575
How about we take turns?

1763
01:09:00,576 --> 01:09:01,946
- Take turns? I'm in.
- Okay.

1764
01:09:02,616 --> 01:09:05,085
Hold on. I need to roll up my sleeves.

1765
01:09:05,086 --> 01:09:06,345
- Are you ready?
- Yes.

1766
01:09:06,346 --> 01:09:07,746
(Letting his forearms do the talking)

1767
01:09:08,516 --> 01:09:09,815
I heard you wanted to become a basketball player.

1768
01:09:09,816 --> 01:09:11,456
I loved basketball.

1769
01:09:12,126 --> 01:09:13,156
Basketball?

1770
01:09:13,726 --> 01:09:15,796
I knew I'd be better than those two.

1771
01:09:17,596 --> 01:09:20,065
In the past, I'd play it whenever I spotted one.

1772
01:09:20,066 --> 01:09:22,936
When I was good at it, I made every shot.

1773
01:09:23,336 --> 01:09:25,706
I totally did. You know the score...

1774
01:09:25,836 --> 01:09:26,905
on the board?

1775
01:09:26,906 --> 01:09:28,335
I went home only after I'd beaten the high score.

1776
01:09:28,336 --> 01:09:30,036
- Really?
- Yes.

1777
01:09:32,076 --> 01:09:34,575
(I'll crush Lee Seo Jin today!)

1778
01:09:34,576 --> 01:09:35,916
Get right up close to the machine.

1779
01:09:36,076 --> 01:09:37,746
Press the button whenever you're ready.

1780
01:09:38,246 --> 01:09:40,345
You must score over 50 points to advance to the 2nd quarter.

1781
01:09:40,346 --> 01:09:42,716
(The 2nd quarter only starts if they break 50 points in the 1st.)

1782
01:09:43,556 --> 01:09:44,986
First quarter starts.

1783
01:09:45,156 --> 01:09:47,086
(He scores as soon as the game begins!)

1784
01:09:47,186 --> 01:09:51,095
Two points!

1785
01:09:51,096 --> 01:09:54,666
(Shot after shot, the ball goes straight into the hoop.)

1786
01:09:55,136 --> 01:09:57,196
Two points!

1787
01:09:57,966 --> 01:10:00,106
- Two points!
- Are you a robot or what?

1788
01:10:00,206 --> 01:10:01,236
Two points!

1789
01:10:01,636 --> 01:10:04,776
(Basketball robot, 9C)

1790
01:10:05,076 --> 01:10:06,106
Two points!

1791
01:10:06,306 --> 01:10:07,605
Here's what's important.

1792
01:10:07,606 --> 01:10:09,746
Use one hand. You shouldn't use both hands.

1793
01:10:09,846 --> 01:10:11,276
You've got to grab the ball with one hand...

1794
01:10:11,586 --> 01:10:12,685
and shoot with the other.

1795
01:10:12,686 --> 01:10:15,056
- Keep that cycle...
- Two points!

1796
01:10:15,416 --> 01:10:17,356
- going.
- Two points!

1797
01:10:17,716 --> 01:10:19,286
Two points!

1798
01:10:19,426 --> 01:10:22,796
(Past 30 points)

1799
01:10:23,156 --> 01:10:25,826
(Feeling anxious)

1800
01:10:27,626 --> 01:10:29,366
(Past 40 points)

1801
01:10:29,566 --> 01:10:30,636
Three points!

1802
01:10:31,266 --> 01:10:32,666
Fifty points!

1803
01:10:33,236 --> 01:10:36,236
Fifty points!

1804
01:10:39,606 --> 01:10:40,675
Three points!

1805
01:10:40,676 --> 01:10:43,776
(He needs over 50 points to clear the 1st quarter!)

1806
01:10:44,476 --> 01:10:49,055
(Suk Ku, the self-proclaimed basketball master)

1807
01:10:49,056 --> 01:10:50,985
(Can he make it past the 1st quarter?)

1808
01:10:50,986 --> 01:10:52,326
- Fifty points!
- Just one more.

1809
01:10:53,556 --> 01:10:55,656
- He did it.
- It's over fifty points.

1810
01:10:56,296 --> 01:10:57,656
Well done.

1811
01:10:58,696 --> 01:11:01,635
(It's over 50 points!)

1812
01:11:01,636 --> 01:11:04,195
- The 2nd quarter!
- The 2nd quarter!

1813
01:11:04,196 --> 01:11:06,336
- My gosh, that was close.
- My gosh.

1814
01:11:06,406 --> 01:11:07,935
Are you ready?

1815
01:11:07,936 --> 01:11:09,436
(The 2nd quarter begins.)

1816
01:11:09,776 --> 01:11:12,976
- Two points!
- The hoop moves.

1817
01:11:14,546 --> 01:11:15,646
Two points!

1818
01:11:16,816 --> 01:11:18,416
Oh, gosh. Why aren't they going in?

1819
01:11:18,586 --> 01:11:20,586
Two points!

1820
01:11:20,886 --> 01:11:22,316
He needs to get 150 points.

1821
01:11:22,686 --> 01:11:24,256
- What?
- He needs to get 150 points.

1822
01:11:24,456 --> 01:11:25,486
Two points!

1823
01:11:25,786 --> 01:11:27,685
Three points!

1824
01:11:27,686 --> 01:11:30,056
(A last-minute flurry of 3-pointers)

1825
01:11:30,156 --> 01:11:31,226
Three points!

1826
01:11:31,596 --> 01:11:32,696
Three points!

1827
01:11:34,426 --> 01:11:36,936
(Past 100 points)

1828
01:11:37,966 --> 01:11:38,966
Three points!

1829
01:11:39,766 --> 01:11:42,235
(He falls short of the record, finishing with 110 points.)

1830
01:11:42,236 --> 01:11:43,306
I couldn't do it.

1831
01:11:43,836 --> 01:11:44,905
Well done.

1832
01:11:44,906 --> 01:11:47,546
(It's now Seo Jin's turn.)

1833
01:11:47,676 --> 01:11:48,916
Back when I was in college,

1834
01:11:49,216 --> 01:11:51,045
- it was Michael Jordan's prime.
- Me too.

1835
01:11:51,046 --> 01:11:52,686
I watched a lot of basketball games.

1836
01:11:53,686 --> 01:11:56,685
Seo Jin loves the US,

1837
01:11:56,686 --> 01:11:58,256
and the US is the home of basketball.

1838
01:11:58,956 --> 01:12:00,686
Seo Jin is my rival.

1839
01:12:02,056 --> 01:12:03,796
Are you ready?

1840
01:12:04,056 --> 01:12:05,626
First quarter starts!

1841
01:12:07,896 --> 01:12:09,096
(No score)

1842
01:12:10,766 --> 01:12:11,906
(No score)

1843
01:12:12,206 --> 01:12:13,605
Don't lean into the machine.

1844
01:12:13,606 --> 01:12:14,665
Oh, no.

1845
01:12:14,666 --> 01:12:16,606
(Slow)

1846
01:12:17,536 --> 01:12:18,546
Two points!

1847
01:12:21,046 --> 01:12:22,175
You move on to the second quarter...

1848
01:12:22,176 --> 01:12:23,316
- if you get 50 points.
- Two points!

1849
01:12:23,676 --> 01:12:25,346
He can't get 50 points.

1850
01:12:25,616 --> 01:12:26,885
Oh, no.

1851
01:12:26,886 --> 01:12:28,785
(50 points feel hopelessly out of reach.)

1852
01:12:28,786 --> 01:12:29,956
He can't do it.

1853
01:12:30,416 --> 01:12:31,656
- He can't.
- Just look.

1854
01:12:33,156 --> 01:12:35,426
(Sweating bullets)

1855
01:12:36,026 --> 01:12:39,066
(Seo Genie's misery is my happiness.)

1856
01:12:40,526 --> 01:12:41,536
Three points!

1857
01:12:42,466 --> 01:12:43,495
See that?

1858
01:12:43,496 --> 01:12:44,965
Twenty-eight points.

1859
01:12:44,966 --> 01:12:47,466
- Gosh.
- Look at the score difference.

1860
01:12:47,806 --> 01:12:50,836
(Dimples of embarrassment)

1861
01:12:50,906 --> 01:12:53,876
Seo Jin was a bit of a disappointment.

1862
01:12:55,416 --> 01:12:56,846
Why couldn't he score more?

1863
01:12:59,546 --> 01:13:01,916
(Disappointed)

1864
01:13:02,156 --> 01:13:03,386
He was a total machine.

1865
01:13:04,486 --> 01:13:05,556
Guns?

1866
01:13:05,886 --> 01:13:08,295
- It's...
- Sergeant Kim.

1867
01:13:08,296 --> 01:13:09,595
- Then...
- Really.

1868
01:13:09,596 --> 01:13:10,956
Let those two have a showdown.

1869
01:13:11,226 --> 01:13:12,565
- What?
- You two have a showdown.

1870
01:13:12,566 --> 01:13:14,466
Okay. With the gun game, right?

1871
01:13:15,496 --> 01:13:16,536
Who's going first?

1872
01:13:17,066 --> 01:13:18,135
- You.
- Me.

1873
01:13:18,136 --> 01:13:19,505
- Who's going first?
- Me.

1874
01:13:19,506 --> 01:13:21,906
- I'll go first.
- You?

1875
01:13:22,836 --> 01:13:25,005
Didn't you two use the same model of gun?

1876
01:13:25,006 --> 01:13:26,475
- What?
- Didn't you shoot a rifle?

1877
01:13:26,476 --> 01:13:28,275
I did. I was an infantryman.

1878
01:13:28,276 --> 01:13:29,315
With our pride as infantrymen...

1879
01:13:29,316 --> 01:13:30,546
- on the line.
- Okay.

1880
01:13:32,686 --> 01:13:34,186
There are targets worth 50 and 70 points.

1881
01:13:35,056 --> 01:13:39,785
(Aiming)

1882
01:13:39,786 --> 01:13:40,886
You didn't hit it.

1883
01:13:41,356 --> 01:13:42,996
- I didn't?
- You didn't.

1884
01:13:44,026 --> 01:13:45,426
- I didn't?
- You didn't.

1885
01:13:46,026 --> 01:13:47,095
You did now.

1886
01:13:47,096 --> 01:13:48,125
(Bull's-eye)

1887
01:13:48,126 --> 01:13:49,866
(50 points)

1888
01:13:50,496 --> 01:13:53,166
(Kwang Kyu is good at shooting.)

1889
01:13:54,536 --> 01:13:56,775
(Sergeant Kim takes each shot carefully.)

1890
01:13:56,776 --> 01:13:58,006
Nice.

1891
01:13:59,076 --> 01:14:00,145
Nice.

1892
01:14:00,146 --> 01:14:02,176
(Well done, Kwang Kyu!)

1893
01:14:02,716 --> 01:14:03,845
(Aiming for the 70-point target)

1894
01:14:03,846 --> 01:14:05,045
(70 points)

1895
01:14:05,046 --> 01:14:06,046
(70 points)

1896
01:14:06,047 --> 01:14:07,115
Nice.

1897
01:14:07,116 --> 01:14:09,816
(70 points)

1898
01:14:13,656 --> 01:14:15,726
(3 bull's-eyes in a row)

1899
01:14:17,456 --> 01:14:18,895
Yes.

1900
01:14:18,896 --> 01:14:20,065
- Really.
- Nine hundred points.

1901
01:14:20,066 --> 01:14:22,035
- Over there.
- One hundred points.

1902
01:14:22,036 --> 01:14:23,535
- Are there more?
- Yes, 100 points.

1903
01:14:23,536 --> 01:14:25,305
- Over there.
- One hundred points.

1904
01:14:25,306 --> 01:14:26,966
- Are there more?
- Yes, 100 points.

1905
01:14:27,566 --> 01:14:29,075
(There's still 1 shot left.)

1906
01:14:29,076 --> 01:14:30,106
(Miss)

1907
01:14:32,906 --> 01:14:33,945
It's over.

1908
01:14:33,946 --> 01:14:35,476
(Too busy showing off, he wastes his last shot.)

1909
01:14:35,616 --> 01:14:37,816
- It's over.
- Come on.

1910
01:14:38,916 --> 01:14:40,315
You lost focus on the last shot.

1911
01:14:40,316 --> 01:14:42,385
My focus... I thought the game was over.

1912
01:14:42,386 --> 01:14:43,815
You're great at it.

1913
01:14:43,816 --> 01:14:45,686
I wasn't used to it.

1914
01:14:45,756 --> 01:14:46,785
- It's been ages.
- Is that so?

1915
01:14:46,786 --> 01:14:48,025
Can you actually shoot with it?

1916
01:14:48,026 --> 01:14:49,326
Hold it out far.

1917
01:14:49,626 --> 01:14:51,625
Wait. It's too tiny.

1918
01:14:51,626 --> 01:14:53,326
- How did you do it?
- It's jealousy.

1919
01:14:53,766 --> 01:14:55,165
I don't think I can do it.

1920
01:14:55,166 --> 01:14:57,596
You have to aim well.

1921
01:14:58,366 --> 01:15:00,666
(I'm getting nervous.)

1922
01:15:00,806 --> 01:15:02,835
Press the button on the right whenever you're ready.

1923
01:15:02,836 --> 01:15:04,136
(The overseas deployment veteran opens fire.)

1924
01:15:05,906 --> 01:15:07,906
It's... 50 points.

1925
01:15:11,076 --> 01:15:12,086
(70 points)

1926
01:15:12,716 --> 01:15:14,085
(Suk Ku is even good at shooting?)

1927
01:15:14,086 --> 01:15:16,556
Suk Ku sure has fired a few guns before.

1928
01:15:22,526 --> 01:15:24,655
(One shot)

1929
01:15:24,656 --> 01:15:26,996
(One kill)

1930
01:15:27,326 --> 01:15:29,896
(Putting the sergeant to shame)

1931
01:15:30,136 --> 01:15:32,036
He's already at 830 points.

1932
01:15:33,436 --> 01:15:37,636
(He's beaten Kwang Kyu's 900 points with 15 shots still left.)

1933
01:15:38,236 --> 01:15:39,305
One hundred points.

1934
01:15:39,306 --> 01:15:41,146
(A moving target worth 100 points)

1935
01:15:41,846 --> 01:15:43,575
(Target spotted)

1936
01:15:43,576 --> 01:15:45,116
(Aim locked in)

1937
01:15:45,486 --> 01:15:47,085
Nice shot.

1938
01:15:47,086 --> 01:15:48,145
(Another moving target)

1939
01:15:48,146 --> 01:15:49,155
Another 100 points.

1940
01:15:49,156 --> 01:15:50,156
(100 points)

1941
01:15:52,526 --> 01:15:54,886
(That qualifies him as an expert marksman, right?)

1942
01:15:55,626 --> 01:15:56,695
Nice shot.

1943
01:15:56,696 --> 01:15:59,766
(Forget the competition. He's just so cool!)

1944
01:16:01,896 --> 01:16:03,795
(Racking up the points)

1945
01:16:03,796 --> 01:16:05,466
One more shot and it's a gold medal.

1946
01:16:06,966 --> 01:16:09,736
(My Star's shooting skills could make anyone fall for him.)

1947
01:16:11,036 --> 01:16:13,076
- It's 1,500 points!
- A gold medal!

1948
01:16:13,406 --> 01:16:16,075
(Hit 1,500 points)

1949
01:16:16,076 --> 01:16:18,076
- Don't you get a prize?
- You do.

1950
01:16:18,316 --> 01:16:19,385
- Really?
- Yes.

1951
01:16:19,386 --> 01:16:21,755
- See?
- It's coming out.

1952
01:16:21,756 --> 01:16:24,986
- It's out.
- Nice.

1953
01:16:25,826 --> 01:16:26,826
What...

1954
01:16:26,827 --> 01:16:30,295
(Dopamine overload)

1955
01:16:30,296 --> 01:16:31,396
Hooray!

1956
01:16:31,826 --> 01:16:33,566
- You're a real marksman.
- As expected.

1957
01:16:33,866 --> 01:16:35,766
Suk Ku is good at everything.

1958
01:16:36,596 --> 01:16:37,596
It was fun.

1959
01:16:40,966 --> 01:16:42,176
- To the side, please.
- Okay.

1960
01:16:42,676 --> 01:16:44,375
- With that, over there.
- Over there?

1961
01:16:44,376 --> 01:16:46,146
(A stroll along Gwangalli Beach with My Star)

1962
01:16:47,746 --> 01:16:49,146
How about we take a selfie?

1963
01:16:49,946 --> 01:16:51,376
Kwang Kyu, let's take a selfie.

1964
01:16:52,186 --> 01:16:54,045
(Together with the plushie)

1965
01:16:54,046 --> 01:16:56,156
We need the bridge in the photo.

1966
01:16:59,356 --> 01:17:00,455
Like so?

1967
01:17:00,456 --> 01:17:01,855
(Gwangalli, My Genie Secretary, I've conquered them all.)

1968
01:17:01,856 --> 01:17:02,956
The bridge is in.

1969
01:17:03,956 --> 01:17:05,266
(Happy)

1970
01:17:06,326 --> 01:17:09,396
I'll hang it there.

1971
01:17:10,536 --> 01:17:12,035
(My Star has a new plushie companion.)

1972
01:17:12,036 --> 01:17:13,136
Thank you.

1973
01:17:16,906 --> 01:17:19,276
(Feeling proud)

1974
01:17:20,006 --> 01:17:21,246
Isn't that Kwang Kyu?

1975
01:17:22,216 --> 01:17:23,815
What does your father do?

1976
01:17:23,816 --> 01:17:24,975
The kid said, "What does your father do?"

1977
01:17:24,976 --> 01:17:26,585
- What does your father do?
- What does your father do?

1978
01:17:26,586 --> 01:17:29,156
Treat your father well.

1979
01:17:30,356 --> 01:17:32,055
Isn't yours, "You've been kidnapped?"

1980
01:17:32,056 --> 01:17:33,855
Mine is, "You've been kidnapped."

1981
01:17:33,856 --> 01:17:34,985
You've been kidnapped.

1982
01:17:34,986 --> 01:17:36,955
- Seo Jin's is, "Does it hurt?"
- "Does it hurt?"

1983
01:17:36,956 --> 01:17:38,896
- "It hurts me too."
- "It hurts me too."

1984
01:17:38,926 --> 01:17:39,966
Please say it.

1985
01:17:40,196 --> 01:17:42,165
- Please say it.
- No.

1986
01:17:42,166 --> 01:17:43,865
- Please say it.
- No.

1987
01:17:43,866 --> 01:17:45,465
- Please say it.
- Do it.

1988
01:17:45,466 --> 01:17:47,665
I haven't asked you to do anything today.

1989
01:17:47,666 --> 01:17:49,335
- Do it for him.
- Isn't that where we're going?

1990
01:17:49,336 --> 01:17:51,475
- Please say it.
- Do it for him.

1991
01:17:51,476 --> 01:17:53,405
Do it. My Star is asking you to do it.

1992
01:17:53,406 --> 01:17:54,406
(Grabbing his arm)

1993
01:17:54,407 --> 01:17:56,075
- Do it for him.
- No.

1994
01:17:56,076 --> 01:17:57,145
Please say it.

1995
01:17:57,146 --> 01:17:59,515
- No way.
- Please.

1996
01:17:59,516 --> 01:18:00,985
- Please say it.
- Are you actually hurt?

1997
01:18:00,986 --> 01:18:02,885
- No.
- Where is it?

1998
01:18:04,166 --> 01:18:05,405
(Time: 5:30pm, Details: A wrap-up party at an ocean view restaurant)

1999
01:18:05,406 --> 01:18:06,966
This is so nice. Oh, my gosh.

2000
01:18:08,606 --> 01:18:11,135
(An uninterrupted view of the Gwangalli beach)

2001
01:18:11,136 --> 01:18:14,006
(They arrive at a restaurant with a spectacular view.)

2002
01:18:14,346 --> 01:18:16,675
(My Star studies the menu.)

2003
01:18:16,676 --> 01:18:18,146
I'm getting a margarita.

2004
01:18:18,346 --> 01:18:19,346
(Impressed)

2005
01:18:19,347 --> 01:18:20,415
Excuse me.

2006
01:18:20,416 --> 01:18:21,416
(A foreign staff member approaches.)

2007
01:18:21,417 --> 01:18:23,255
Hi.

2008
01:18:23,256 --> 01:18:24,356
Do you speak Korean?

2009
01:18:25,726 --> 01:18:27,086
(Instinctively avoiding eye contact)

2010
01:18:27,156 --> 01:18:29,055
What's your signature? Quesadilla?

2011
01:18:29,056 --> 01:18:30,695
Yes, quesadilla and pizza.

2012
01:18:30,696 --> 01:18:33,095
They're the most ordered foods.

2013
01:18:33,096 --> 01:18:34,565
- Is that so? Where are you from?
- Okay.

2014
01:18:34,566 --> 01:18:35,566
I'm from Italy.

2015
01:18:35,567 --> 01:18:36,866
- Italy?
- Yes.

2016
01:18:36,936 --> 01:18:38,166
So I'm guessing pizza.

2017
01:18:38,496 --> 01:18:39,966
Pizza? What kind of pizza?

2018
01:18:40,366 --> 01:18:42,606
- Pepperoni and combination.
- Pepperoni? Okay.

2019
01:18:42,836 --> 01:18:44,676
- Pepperoni?
- I'm in.

2020
01:18:45,006 --> 01:18:46,746
One pepperoni.

2021
01:18:46,946 --> 01:18:51,075
Can I, then, for a drink, have a margarita?

2022
01:18:51,076 --> 01:18:53,386
- Two? Three?
- Three margaritas.

2023
01:18:53,816 --> 01:18:56,086
(Tilting his head)

2024
01:18:57,086 --> 01:18:58,556
- Good?
- Yes.

2025
01:18:59,386 --> 01:19:01,155
Okay. Good.

2026
01:19:01,156 --> 01:19:03,096
(Putting every English word he knows to work)

2027
01:19:04,496 --> 01:19:06,826
I was asked to call Ji Min,

2028
01:19:07,326 --> 01:19:08,396
but I said no.

2029
01:19:09,596 --> 01:19:11,736
Call Ji Min? Why?

2030
01:19:12,336 --> 01:19:13,505
- You do it.
- What?

2031
01:19:13,506 --> 01:19:14,535
You call her.

2032
01:19:14,536 --> 01:19:15,836
She likes it when you call her.

2033
01:19:15,976 --> 01:19:18,135
- She doesn't really like me.
- What?

2034
01:19:18,136 --> 01:19:19,305
She doesn't like him either.

2035
01:19:19,306 --> 01:19:20,605
- I...
- She practically loves him.

2036
01:19:20,606 --> 01:19:22,346
Ji Min might not answer the phone.

2037
01:19:23,376 --> 01:19:24,515
- Is it on speaker?
- Yes.

2038
01:19:24,516 --> 01:19:25,586
The volume is too low.

2039
01:19:26,186 --> 01:19:27,485
- Turn it up.
- After drinks...

2040
01:19:27,486 --> 01:19:29,556
- Hey, Kwang Kyu.
- My Star.

2041
01:19:29,756 --> 01:19:31,716
- Kwang Kyu.
- I heard you were in Haeundae.

2042
01:19:32,686 --> 01:19:34,325
Me? I'm in Busan right now.

2043
01:19:34,326 --> 01:19:36,095
- Are you in Busan?
- Yes.

2044
01:19:36,096 --> 01:19:40,765
Your favorites, Lee Seo Jin and Suk Ku, are here. Come on over.

2045
01:19:40,766 --> 01:19:42,235
I think you've got the wrong number.

2046
01:19:42,236 --> 01:19:44,595
Wait. Why?

2047
01:19:44,596 --> 01:19:46,465
Why are you saying that?

2048
01:19:46,466 --> 01:19:48,675
Didn't you show him who's boss recently?

2049
01:19:48,676 --> 01:19:50,506
Throw him into the ocean.

2050
01:19:51,506 --> 01:19:54,076
I have no reason to throw him into the ocean.

2051
01:19:54,476 --> 01:19:55,645
Kick him into the water.

2052
01:19:55,646 --> 01:19:56,915
What about Suk Ku?

2053
01:19:56,916 --> 01:19:58,016
And Suk Ku?

2054
01:19:58,746 --> 01:20:01,145
Suk Ku is something like...

2055
01:20:01,146 --> 01:20:03,286
Seo Jin's successor.

2056
01:20:03,816 --> 01:20:05,755
Is that so?

2057
01:20:05,756 --> 01:20:08,286
- Yes, I...
- Hey, Ji Min.

2058
01:20:08,456 --> 01:20:10,396
Who just said, "Hey, Ji Min?"

2059
01:20:10,456 --> 01:20:11,526
It's me, Suk Ku.

2060
01:20:11,996 --> 01:20:13,126
You must've lost it.

2061
01:20:15,096 --> 01:20:18,596
Isn't it about time we became friends?

2062
01:20:18,966 --> 01:20:20,105
No.

2063
01:20:20,106 --> 01:20:21,735
(Born in November 1982, Born in February 1983)

2064
01:20:21,736 --> 01:20:22,836
Don't you dare.

2065
01:20:23,006 --> 01:20:24,606
Our birthdays aren't that far apart.

2066
01:20:25,276 --> 01:20:27,346
(Ji Min is still the same as ever.)

2067
01:20:27,546 --> 01:20:30,976
Suk Ku, you're putting them to good use, right?

2068
01:20:31,376 --> 01:20:34,616
I think I get along with Seo Jin really well.

2069
01:20:35,186 --> 01:20:37,885
Right? Even I can see that you two are two peas in a pod.

2070
01:20:37,886 --> 01:20:39,555
That's why...

2071
01:20:39,556 --> 01:20:42,556
Kwang Kyu had a tough time today.

2072
01:20:42,926 --> 01:20:45,365
Really? Take good care of Kwang Kyu, will you?

2073
01:20:45,366 --> 01:20:46,366
What?

2074
01:20:46,367 --> 01:20:48,296
- Ji Min.
- Yes?

2075
01:20:48,566 --> 01:20:51,336
It's like Suk Ku and Seo Jin are dating.

2076
01:20:52,066 --> 01:20:53,405
The two are on the same wavelength.

2077
01:20:53,406 --> 01:20:55,636
(All his pent-up hurt comes pouring out.)

2078
01:20:55,706 --> 01:20:57,506
Come over and take my side.

2079
01:20:57,976 --> 01:21:00,376
Kwang Kyu, I need to get going now.

2080
01:21:00,706 --> 01:21:03,216
- Right now?
- What time do you finish?

2081
01:21:03,276 --> 01:21:04,716
What event are you attending today?

2082
01:21:05,346 --> 01:21:06,416
- Me?
- Yes.

2083
01:21:06,746 --> 01:21:07,846
Mind your own business.

2084
01:21:08,856 --> 01:21:09,856
- See?
- Okay.

2085
01:21:09,857 --> 01:21:11,185
(Shut down instantly)

2086
01:21:11,186 --> 01:21:13,956
Why don't you come over for a drink before you leave, if you have time?

2087
01:21:14,526 --> 01:21:15,595
(Laughing)

2088
01:21:15,596 --> 01:21:18,656
- Come over, Ji Min.
- I only drink with people I like.

2089
01:21:19,566 --> 01:21:21,865
(That rules them out.)

2090
01:21:21,866 --> 01:21:23,265
I'm hanging up.

2091
01:21:23,266 --> 01:21:25,065
- Okay, bye.
- Bye.

2092
01:21:25,066 --> 01:21:26,236
Bye.

2093
01:21:26,866 --> 01:21:28,566
Show some respect, Son Suk Ku.

2094
01:21:30,776 --> 01:21:32,076
Good luck today.

2095
01:21:32,206 --> 01:21:33,506
Bye.

2096
01:21:33,906 --> 01:21:35,345
- Suk Ku...
- It's my first time seeing her...

2097
01:21:35,346 --> 01:21:36,745
treat someone other than me like that.

2098
01:21:36,746 --> 01:21:38,176
Suk Ku must've gotten on her bad side.

2099
01:21:38,676 --> 01:21:40,645
(He's just like me, after all.)

2100
01:21:40,646 --> 01:21:43,856
It's surprising that there's another guy like me in Ji Min's life.

2101
01:21:44,286 --> 01:21:47,286
Looking at him made me think, "He'll turn out like me soon."

2102
01:21:47,986 --> 01:21:50,626
(A perfect pair, as expected)

2103
01:21:51,796 --> 01:21:53,765
(Wide-eyed)

2104
01:21:53,766 --> 01:21:54,926
Are those margaritas?

2105
01:21:55,296 --> 01:21:56,696
They're huge.

2106
01:21:56,836 --> 01:21:58,336
I didn't think they'd be this huge.

2107
01:21:58,766 --> 01:22:01,405
- It looks good.
- Here. Cheers.

2108
01:22:01,406 --> 01:22:03,975
- My Star, great work today.
- Great work.

2109
01:22:03,976 --> 01:22:06,306
- Great work.
- Thank you. Great work.

2110
01:22:06,646 --> 01:22:08,046
This is a first for me.

2111
01:22:09,176 --> 01:22:11,576
You don't drink a margarita through a straw.

2112
01:22:11,676 --> 01:22:13,146
Sip it from the salted rim.

2113
01:22:13,446 --> 01:22:14,816
I didn't think they'd be this huge.

2114
01:22:15,516 --> 01:22:17,955
(A refreshing sip washes away the day's fatigue.)

2115
01:22:17,956 --> 01:22:20,185
- It's...
- This margarita barely has a kick.

2116
01:22:20,186 --> 01:22:22,295
- It's like juice.
- Exactly.

2117
01:22:22,296 --> 01:22:23,356
(Just to My Star's taste)

2118
01:22:23,926 --> 01:22:25,566
Do you take breaks, Suk Ku?

2119
01:22:26,296 --> 01:22:27,595
I do these days.

2120
01:22:27,596 --> 01:22:28,896
- You do?
- Yes.

2121
01:22:29,866 --> 01:22:30,866
What about you?

2122
01:22:31,196 --> 01:22:32,435
I'm always on a break.

2123
01:22:32,436 --> 01:22:33,436
(Must you ask?)

2124
01:22:33,437 --> 01:22:34,606
He's got no work.

2125
01:22:35,236 --> 01:22:36,305
What do you do these days?

2126
01:22:36,306 --> 01:22:38,476
Searching for a movie to watch is such a hassle...

2127
01:22:39,006 --> 01:22:41,246
that I just leave the TV on a movie channel.

2128
01:22:41,776 --> 01:22:44,775
Movies play one after another, like "The Man from Nowhere."

2129
01:22:44,776 --> 01:22:45,886
Do you only watch Korean movies?

2130
01:22:46,746 --> 01:22:48,316
Korean movies are fun.

2131
01:22:49,416 --> 01:22:50,815
Do you rarely watch foreign movies?

2132
01:22:50,816 --> 01:22:52,056
I watch them,

2133
01:22:52,256 --> 01:22:54,486
- but I have to read the subtitles.
- Right.

2134
01:22:55,596 --> 01:22:58,555
It must be nice for you two since you understand English right away.

2135
01:22:58,556 --> 01:22:59,595
You don't have to read the subtitles.

2136
01:22:59,596 --> 01:23:00,626
- Right?
- I read the subtitles.

2137
01:23:00,766 --> 01:23:02,165
- It's hard to understand.
- What?

2138
01:23:02,166 --> 01:23:05,395
After talking to someone in English for an hour,

2139
01:23:05,396 --> 01:23:06,406
my head hurts.

2140
01:23:07,806 --> 01:23:09,705
- I totally get it.
- Right?

2141
01:23:09,706 --> 01:23:12,576
- Your head hurts?
- It takes so much brainpower.

2142
01:23:12,706 --> 01:23:14,175
- Is that so?
- I get drained.

2143
01:23:14,176 --> 01:23:15,176
Exactly.

2144
01:23:15,177 --> 01:23:18,576
So when talking to Americans or other English speakers,

2145
01:23:19,186 --> 01:23:21,115
I can understand them.

2146
01:23:21,116 --> 01:23:23,285
But I can choose not to if I don't want to.

2147
01:23:23,286 --> 01:23:24,615
(How?)

2148
01:23:24,616 --> 01:23:27,055
I only understand if I make a conscious effort.

2149
01:23:27,056 --> 01:23:29,756
Otherwise, English just sounds like birds chirping.

2150
01:23:30,926 --> 01:23:32,426
I can't understand a thing.

2151
01:23:32,626 --> 01:23:33,865
You're in a much better situation.

2152
01:23:33,866 --> 01:23:35,025
- What?
- Since you can't understand,

2153
01:23:35,026 --> 01:23:36,236
you don't have to use your brain.

2154
01:23:37,266 --> 01:23:38,335
You're better off that way.

2155
01:23:38,336 --> 01:23:39,535
Fine.

2156
01:23:39,536 --> 01:23:40,965
(I should've known there was a catch.)

2157
01:23:40,966 --> 01:23:43,506
It's way better not to be able to understand anything.

2158
01:23:44,706 --> 01:23:47,506
Have you two ever actually fought?

2159
01:23:48,046 --> 01:23:49,915
(Have we ever actually fought?)

2160
01:23:49,916 --> 01:23:51,115
Like an actual fight?

2161
01:23:51,116 --> 01:23:53,986
- For example, one day, - Yes?

2162
01:23:54,086 --> 01:23:57,185
Kwang Kyu comes up and says, "Hey,"

2163
01:23:57,186 --> 01:23:58,585
and the atmosphere turns cold.

2164
01:23:58,586 --> 01:24:00,956
I'd tell him, "Bring it on."

2165
01:24:03,056 --> 01:24:04,425
Then we'd totally fight for real.

2166
01:24:04,426 --> 01:24:06,495
There was a time when I got angry...

2167
01:24:06,496 --> 01:24:08,935
- and wanted to teach him a lesson.
- Have you tried?

2168
01:24:08,936 --> 01:24:11,496
- Have you tried?
- Yes, I lost my temper.

2169
01:24:12,436 --> 01:24:13,436
You did?

2170
01:24:13,437 --> 01:24:15,605
- You may not remember it.
- I see.

2171
01:24:15,606 --> 01:24:17,276
I grabbed him by the collar.

2172
01:24:19,446 --> 01:24:21,246
But Seo Jin was super strong.

2173
01:24:22,646 --> 01:24:23,975
Guys can tell...

2174
01:24:23,976 --> 01:24:25,415
the moment they grab someone.

2175
01:24:25,416 --> 01:24:28,715
Honestly, it's over before you even grab them by the collar.

2176
01:24:28,716 --> 01:24:30,286
You can tell right away.

2177
01:24:30,616 --> 01:24:32,255
Seo Jin is surprisingly strong.

2178
01:24:32,256 --> 01:24:33,325
(He knew he'd lost right away.)

2179
01:24:33,326 --> 01:24:34,656
And so, I just...

2180
01:24:38,426 --> 01:24:41,966
I used to do a lot of weight training.

2181
01:24:42,496 --> 01:24:44,035
I don't do much now.

2182
01:24:44,036 --> 01:24:46,436
Suk Ku, you must still be working with a personal trainer, right?

2183
01:24:46,906 --> 01:24:48,936
Didn't you bulk up for "The Roundup?"

2184
01:24:49,136 --> 01:24:50,376
Back then...

2185
01:24:50,706 --> 01:24:52,805
- Back then...
- I could tell as soon as I saw it.

2186
01:24:52,806 --> 01:24:54,875
Back then, I only did weight training.

2187
01:24:54,876 --> 01:24:56,346
(He focused on weight training to bulk up.)

2188
01:24:56,746 --> 01:24:58,345
When I saw you back then, your body was...

2189
01:24:58,346 --> 01:24:59,386
(Got sauce on him)

2190
01:24:59,546 --> 01:25:00,685
- Oh, no.
- It looked like...

2191
01:25:00,686 --> 01:25:01,815
Suk Ku worked out without a diet restriction.

2192
01:25:01,816 --> 01:25:02,856
(Sucking off the sauce)

2193
01:25:03,686 --> 01:25:05,855
- Why are you sucking on your tie?
- I dropped some sauce.

2194
01:25:05,856 --> 01:25:07,255
(My Star is a macho man.)

2195
01:25:07,256 --> 01:25:08,726
(Quickly coming to Suk Ku's rescue)

2196
01:25:08,956 --> 01:25:11,626
But bulking up was the right move for that role.

2197
01:25:12,396 --> 01:25:13,565
It would be weird...

2198
01:25:13,566 --> 01:25:14,696
- if you were nothing but muscles.
- Exactly.

2199
01:25:14,766 --> 01:25:17,236
You know how sometimes an actor showing off his abs...

2200
01:25:17,536 --> 01:25:19,205
stands out more...

2201
01:25:19,206 --> 01:25:21,165
than his lines in a movie?

2202
01:25:21,166 --> 01:25:22,406
That's weird.

2203
01:25:22,636 --> 01:25:24,376
When actors have abs...

2204
01:25:24,806 --> 01:25:26,145
that don't fit the role,

2205
01:25:26,146 --> 01:25:28,076
- I hate it.
- It's really weird.

2206
01:25:28,646 --> 01:25:30,115
But you have abs...

2207
01:25:30,116 --> 01:25:31,716
when you shoot bed scenes.

2208
01:25:32,346 --> 01:25:33,945
I've never filmed a bed scene.

2209
01:25:33,946 --> 01:25:35,515
Is that so? Then...

2210
01:25:35,516 --> 01:25:36,916
Have you only done kissing scenes?

2211
01:25:37,386 --> 01:25:38,785
You've never filmed a bed scene?

2212
01:25:38,786 --> 01:25:40,855
I don't think I've ever filmed one.

2213
01:25:40,856 --> 01:25:41,956
Is that so?

2214
01:25:42,626 --> 01:25:45,396
You got in great shape for your bed scene, didn't you?

2215
01:25:46,696 --> 01:25:48,396
I even had a bed scene with a guy.

2216
01:25:48,796 --> 01:25:49,965
- For real?
- With a guy?

2217
01:25:49,966 --> 01:25:51,795
That must be why gay men love you.

2218
01:25:51,796 --> 01:25:53,036
Maybe that's why.

2219
01:25:53,336 --> 01:25:55,066
What was that?

2220
01:25:55,606 --> 01:25:56,606
There was a poll...

2221
01:25:56,607 --> 01:25:58,635
where gay men voted...

2222
01:25:58,636 --> 01:26:00,145
for their ideal type.

2223
01:26:00,146 --> 01:26:01,506
Among gay men?

2224
01:26:01,576 --> 01:26:02,775
Are you currently in first place?

2225
01:26:02,776 --> 01:26:04,146
No, it was just that one time.

2226
01:26:04,616 --> 01:26:06,616
Ji Jin Hee always came in first place,

2227
01:26:06,946 --> 01:26:08,216
but then Suk Ku took his spot.

2228
01:26:08,846 --> 01:26:10,816
Does he give off that vibe?

2229
01:26:11,356 --> 01:26:12,986
Both Ji Jin Hee and Suk Ku...

2230
01:26:13,056 --> 01:26:14,155
are well-built.

2231
01:26:14,156 --> 01:26:15,226
Of course.

2232
01:26:15,326 --> 01:26:17,256
- I was in an independent film.
- I see.

2233
01:26:17,656 --> 01:26:19,965
That director shot...

2234
01:26:19,966 --> 01:26:22,565
a 7-minute scene in 1 take.

2235
01:26:22,566 --> 01:26:23,596
(A full 7 minutes, filmed in 1 take)

2236
01:26:23,666 --> 01:26:25,195
A seven-minute scene is super long.

2237
01:26:25,196 --> 01:26:26,866
It's too long.

2238
01:26:27,206 --> 01:26:28,936
Ultimately, most of the scene was edited out.

2239
01:26:29,106 --> 01:26:30,975
It barely made it into the movie.

2240
01:26:30,976 --> 01:26:32,676
Only 20 seconds made it in.

2241
01:26:32,776 --> 01:26:35,105
Just imagining it is already tough.

2242
01:26:35,106 --> 01:26:37,416
You know, kissing a guy.

2243
01:26:37,516 --> 01:26:38,845
Have you tried kissing one?

2244
01:26:38,846 --> 01:26:39,945
- A guy?
- Yes.

2245
01:26:39,946 --> 01:26:41,146
Have you gone mad?

2246
01:26:41,386 --> 01:26:43,615
Let's say it's an amazing project and the role calls for it.

2247
01:26:43,616 --> 01:26:44,685
- No way.
- It's a great work.

2248
01:26:44,686 --> 01:26:45,686
- For real.
- I'm not doing it.

2249
01:26:45,687 --> 01:26:46,755
- If an Academy Award is guaranteed?
- The director...

2250
01:26:46,756 --> 01:26:48,155
of "Damo" asked you.

2251
01:26:48,156 --> 01:26:49,725
- I'm not doing it.
- Even for an award?

2252
01:26:49,726 --> 01:26:50,755
No.

2253
01:26:50,756 --> 01:26:52,256
I don't even want an Academy Award.

2254
01:26:52,596 --> 01:26:53,725
- Really?
- Yes.

2255
01:26:53,726 --> 01:26:54,796
I'm not doing it.

2256
01:26:55,166 --> 01:26:56,466
What if you were paid a lot?

2257
01:26:57,266 --> 01:26:58,396
- Paid?
- Yes.

2258
01:26:59,166 --> 01:27:00,565
(Thinking)

2259
01:27:00,566 --> 01:27:01,566
Gosh.

2260
01:27:01,567 --> 01:27:02,935
You'll get 100 million dollars.

2261
01:27:02,936 --> 01:27:04,505
(You'll get 100 million dollars.)

2262
01:27:04,506 --> 01:27:06,345
Of course, I'd do it.

2263
01:27:06,346 --> 01:27:07,706
(Smiling brightly)

2264
01:27:08,076 --> 01:27:09,116
Money is everything.

2265
01:27:10,346 --> 01:27:12,116
He's the definition of capitalism.

2266
01:27:13,786 --> 01:27:15,346
If it's 150 million dollars...

2267
01:27:16,586 --> 01:27:17,586
Is that so?

2268
01:27:17,587 --> 01:27:18,785
- I'd film even in a naked state.
- I see.

2269
01:27:18,786 --> 01:27:21,186
(The guy who will kiss for 150 million dollars)

2270
01:27:21,286 --> 01:27:22,555
I'd kiss for ten minutes.

2271
01:27:22,556 --> 01:27:24,356
(3 extra minutes)

2272
01:27:24,856 --> 01:27:26,395
If you were given 150 million dollars,

2273
01:27:26,396 --> 01:27:28,466
could you even kiss Kwang Kyu?

2274
01:27:29,836 --> 01:27:30,936
(Laughing)

2275
01:27:33,836 --> 01:27:35,905
You guys are one of a kind,

2276
01:27:35,906 --> 01:27:37,336
asking the most ridiculous questions.

2277
01:27:38,460 --> 01:27:39,860
I'd do it for 150 million dollars.

2278
01:27:39,930 --> 01:27:41,999
(Seo Jin can even kiss Kwang Kyu for 150 million dollars.)

2279
01:27:42,000 --> 01:27:43,030
Right?

2280
01:27:43,976 --> 01:27:45,776
- I'm not doing it.
- With me?

2281
01:27:45,806 --> 01:27:46,806
What do you have to lose...

2282
01:27:46,806 --> 01:27:47,806
- by kissing me?
- I...

2283
01:27:48,246 --> 01:27:49,976
You have nothing to lose.

2284
01:27:50,216 --> 01:27:53,316
- I'm picky about looks.
- Goodness gracious.

2285
01:27:53,716 --> 01:27:55,145
Kwang Kyu would...

2286
01:27:55,146 --> 01:27:57,786
do it even for 15 million dollars. Cut the nonsense.

2287
01:27:57,956 --> 01:27:59,785
He'd even do it for 150,000 dollars.

2288
01:27:59,786 --> 01:28:01,055
No way. I won't.

2289
01:28:01,056 --> 01:28:02,825
- Stop lying.
- I won't do it.

2290
01:28:02,826 --> 01:28:03,956
I won't.

2291
01:28:05,956 --> 01:28:07,896
I lived alone from middle school onward,

2292
01:28:07,996 --> 01:28:10,166
so I got tired of it early on.

2293
01:28:10,336 --> 01:28:11,566
But now that...

2294
01:28:12,036 --> 01:28:14,306
I've been living with my brother for over ten years,

2295
01:28:14,536 --> 01:28:16,705
I want to...

2296
01:28:16,706 --> 01:28:17,936
live alone again.

2297
01:28:18,306 --> 01:28:19,576
Are you second brothers?

2298
01:28:19,946 --> 01:28:21,275
I...

2299
01:28:21,276 --> 01:28:22,946
What does "second brothers" even mean?

2300
01:28:25,446 --> 01:28:26,515
I have one sibling.

2301
01:28:26,516 --> 01:28:28,245
- A younger brother.
- He has a younger brother.

2302
01:28:28,246 --> 01:28:29,886
- So you're second brothers.
- Right.

2303
01:28:29,916 --> 01:28:31,016
Not three.

2304
01:28:31,086 --> 01:28:33,015
I've heard of "3 brothers," but never "2nd brothers."

2305
01:28:33,016 --> 01:28:35,125
- That's 2nd brothers.
- Don't people say "2 brothers?"

2306
01:28:35,126 --> 01:28:36,155
- No.
- No.

2307
01:28:36,156 --> 01:28:38,055
I have a brother, so we're two brothers.

2308
01:28:38,056 --> 01:28:39,356
(No.)

2309
01:28:39,896 --> 01:28:41,225
(Finding it absurd)

2310
01:28:41,226 --> 01:28:43,295
You two sure get along really well.

2311
01:28:43,296 --> 01:28:45,096
You two get along seriously well.

2312
01:28:45,866 --> 01:28:47,205
You don't say "first brothers."

2313
01:28:47,206 --> 01:28:48,566
- No.
- Exactly.

2314
01:28:48,666 --> 01:28:49,936
It's "two brothers."

2315
01:28:50,606 --> 01:28:51,706
What is it?

2316
01:28:51,876 --> 01:28:53,305
- And "three brothers."
- The thing is,

2317
01:28:53,306 --> 01:28:55,575
it's not easy for two brothers to live together.

2318
01:28:55,576 --> 01:28:56,716
(Changing the subject)

2319
01:28:56,846 --> 01:28:58,645
- We used to fight a lot.
- Is that so?

2320
01:28:58,646 --> 01:29:00,345
- The fights were...
- Didn't you exchange blows?

2321
01:29:00,346 --> 01:29:01,946
We fought...

2322
01:29:02,086 --> 01:29:03,615
so badly that...

2323
01:29:03,616 --> 01:29:05,515
it nearly tore our family apart.

2324
01:29:05,516 --> 01:29:07,255
- What's the age gap?
- Two years.

2325
01:29:07,256 --> 01:29:08,626
Two years is...

2326
01:29:09,386 --> 01:29:10,696
It's the worst.

2327
01:29:10,896 --> 01:29:13,266
My second older brother and I are two years apart.

2328
01:29:13,326 --> 01:29:14,666
We fought like crazy.

2329
01:29:15,396 --> 01:29:17,395
I went bald because he pulled my hair out.

2330
01:29:17,396 --> 01:29:18,835
(I went bald because he pulled my hair out.)

2331
01:29:18,836 --> 01:29:21,266
(Kwang Kyu's killer look, courtesy of his brother)

2332
01:29:21,606 --> 01:29:23,806
"Father, have pity on me."

2333
01:29:23,906 --> 01:29:25,776
I wanted to be...

2334
01:29:26,006 --> 01:29:28,975
over 180cm tall.

2335
01:29:28,976 --> 01:29:30,975
Same here. I still do.

2336
01:29:30,976 --> 01:29:32,016
Right?

2337
01:29:32,076 --> 01:29:34,645
To this day, I think I might've grown taller than 180cm...

2338
01:29:34,646 --> 01:29:36,346
if I'd corrected my bow legs.

2339
01:29:36,586 --> 01:29:38,556
Of all the men...

2340
01:29:39,016 --> 01:29:41,056
in my family,

2341
01:29:41,086 --> 01:29:43,595
I'm the only one who didn't grow taller than 180cm.

2342
01:29:43,596 --> 01:29:45,025
(Suk Ku is the only one under 180cm.)

2343
01:29:45,026 --> 01:29:47,466
What's more,

2344
01:29:47,496 --> 01:29:49,965
I've been the only one in my family...

2345
01:29:49,966 --> 01:29:52,266
with monolids since I was a kid.

2346
01:29:53,236 --> 01:29:55,265
It broke my heart when I was young.

2347
01:29:55,266 --> 01:29:57,706
"Why am I the only short one with small eyes?"

2348
01:29:58,006 --> 01:29:59,805
I had thoughts like that.

2349
01:29:59,806 --> 01:30:02,946
We're in the same boat. Goodness.

2350
01:30:03,916 --> 01:30:05,845
How are you two in the same boat?

2351
01:30:05,846 --> 01:30:07,245
Of the three brothers,

2352
01:30:07,246 --> 01:30:09,316
I'm the only one like this.

2353
01:30:09,546 --> 01:30:12,986
(Kwang Kyu has finally found something in common with My Star.)

2354
01:30:13,526 --> 01:30:15,425
As an actor, Suk Ku is...

2355
01:30:15,426 --> 01:30:17,956
so charming whenever I watch his work.

2356
01:30:18,096 --> 01:30:21,426
He's a guy with many talents and skills.

2357
01:30:22,266 --> 01:30:24,466
Son Suk Ku is still going strong.

2358
01:30:25,496 --> 01:30:27,735
He hasn't fizzled out like Lee Seo Jin.

2359
01:30:27,736 --> 01:30:29,266
(Still holding a grudge)

2360
01:30:30,336 --> 01:30:31,535
- An overall review?
- Yes.

2361
01:30:31,536 --> 01:30:32,936
(How was the care you received today overall?)

2362
01:30:33,306 --> 01:30:34,946
A day to remember...

2363
01:30:35,776 --> 01:30:36,946
in Busan.

2364
01:30:37,976 --> 01:30:39,646
Who would you like as your manager for a month?

2365
01:30:40,046 --> 01:30:41,246
- My manager for a month?
- Yes.

2366
01:30:41,816 --> 01:30:46,055
(Thinking hard)

2367
01:30:46,056 --> 01:30:47,256
I'd choose Lee Seo Jin.

2368
01:30:47,386 --> 01:30:48,486
- Why?
- As expected.

2369
01:30:48,886 --> 01:30:51,056
You don't have to lump us together.

2370
01:30:51,756 --> 01:30:53,625
But I feel like we get along well.

2371
01:30:53,626 --> 01:30:56,526
(My Star only has eyes for Seo Jin.)

2372
01:30:57,436 --> 01:30:59,536
(Bonus clip ahead)

2373
01:31:00,166 --> 01:31:02,306
(Rummaging)

2374
01:31:02,706 --> 01:31:04,176
Use this, Suk Ku.

2375
01:31:05,036 --> 01:31:06,376
- What is it?
- What?

2376
01:31:06,846 --> 01:31:07,976
Use my room.

2377
01:31:08,506 --> 01:31:09,576
Really?

2378
01:31:10,146 --> 01:31:11,976
- Until when?
- Tomorrow.

2379
01:31:12,046 --> 01:31:13,686
- Really?
- Checkout is tomorrow, right?

2380
01:31:14,346 --> 01:31:16,085
I got a corner suite.

2381
01:31:16,086 --> 01:31:18,515
(Genie invites him to his suite.)

2382
01:31:18,516 --> 01:31:20,855
- Take care of it yourself.
- Okay.

2383
01:31:20,856 --> 01:31:21,885
(The Gwangalli bromance continues.)

2384
01:31:21,886 --> 01:31:23,026
- I'll hang out there.
- Good.

2385
01:31:25,326 --> 01:31:26,456
Does it hurt?

2386
01:31:26,696 --> 01:31:27,796
Yes.

2387
01:31:28,326 --> 01:31:29,526
It hurts me too.

2388
01:31:33,166 --> 01:31:35,206
(This feels like a dream.)

2389
01:31:35,306 --> 01:31:37,305
(You know, spending time with him...)

2390
01:31:37,306 --> 01:31:39,576
(and filming a show with him...)

2391
01:31:39,676 --> 01:31:42,176
(This is my first time being on a show with her.)

2392
01:31:42,246 --> 01:31:43,975
(This is the first time I've shared...)

2393
01:31:43,976 --> 01:31:45,376
(the screen with her since then.)

2394
01:31:45,546 --> 01:31:48,546
(We wanted to work with you since Season 1.)

2395
01:31:49,286 --> 01:31:51,456
(Everyone has been waiting for this encounter.)

2396
01:31:51,616 --> 01:31:54,086
(Chae Ok has returned. My Star, Ha Ji Won)

2397
01:31:54,826 --> 01:31:56,356
(Spotted her)

2398
01:31:56,696 --> 01:32:00,696
(The 2 reunite on My Genie Secretary after 23 years.)

2399
01:32:00,896 --> 01:32:03,296
(We might be shooting "Damo" again.)

2400
01:32:03,366 --> 01:32:05,496
(My Genie Secretary's first overseas business trip)

2401
01:32:05,596 --> 01:32:09,266
(In Singapore)

2402
01:32:09,366 --> 01:32:10,535
(Doesn't Ji Won look much prettier now?)

2403
01:32:10,536 --> 01:32:11,936
(Stop it.)

2404
01:32:11,976 --> 01:32:13,906
(She wasn't this pretty in the past.)

2405
01:32:14,046 --> 01:32:15,545
(My Star has dolled up.)

2406
01:32:15,546 --> 01:32:17,215
(- Who are you?
- Stop it.)

2407
01:32:17,216 --> 01:32:18,315
(Don't these look good together?)

2408
01:32:18,316 --> 01:32:19,775
(Ji Won, do you need some sunglasses?)

2409
01:32:19,776 --> 01:32:21,386
(Is the Captain buying them for me?)

2410
01:32:21,686 --> 01:32:23,885
(Even after all the jokes, he does anything for My Star.)

2411
01:32:23,886 --> 01:32:25,855
(Ji Won's eyes have lit up.)

2412
01:32:25,856 --> 01:32:26,885
(She was always like...)

2413
01:32:26,886 --> 01:32:27,985
(Looking dead)

2414
01:32:27,986 --> 01:32:29,656
(Before long, they're bickering.)

2415
01:32:29,726 --> 01:32:31,025
(Who left the most lasting impression...)

2416
01:32:31,026 --> 01:32:32,125
(among all her male co-stars?)

2417
01:32:32,126 --> 01:32:34,126
(Tell us who made the best and worst impressions.)

2418
01:32:34,166 --> 01:32:35,565
(Thinking)

2419
01:32:35,566 --> 01:32:37,435
(Mr. Officer is nervous.)

2420
01:32:37,436 --> 01:32:40,065
(The chemistry with Damo and the officer is still going strong.)

2421
01:32:40,066 --> 01:32:42,266
(And the pinnacle of motorsport, F1)

2422
01:32:42,466 --> 01:32:45,035
(My Star Ji Won has been invited to experience it firsthand.)

2423
01:32:45,036 --> 01:32:47,276
(Thanks to My Star, the secretaries get to watch F1 in person too.)

2424
01:32:47,506 --> 01:32:48,905
(A first on Korean television)

2425
01:32:48,906 --> 01:32:50,416
(Inside the world of F1)

2426
01:32:50,576 --> 01:32:52,176
(The ultimate goal at F1)

2427
01:32:52,276 --> 01:32:53,385
(Is it to meet Max?)

2428
01:32:53,386 --> 01:32:54,616
(Secretaries, make it happen!)

2429
01:32:54,746 --> 01:32:57,086
(I'll try, even if I get run over by a Ferrari.)

2430
01:32:57,186 --> 01:33:00,186
(She wants to meet some F1 drivers.)

2431
01:33:00,286 --> 01:33:01,426
(Is it possible?)

2432
01:33:01,686 --> 01:33:03,056
(Isn't that Max?)

2433
01:33:03,256 --> 01:33:05,656
(Will My Star get to meet her favorite driver?)

2434
01:33:05,856 --> 01:33:08,365
(And...)

2435
01:33:08,366 --> 01:33:11,536
(A modern-day "Damo" romance blossoms amid the F1 action.)

2436
01:33:11,936 --> 01:33:13,466
(Glancing)

2437
01:33:14,006 --> 01:33:15,535
(How will their reunion after 23 years...)

2438
01:33:15,536 --> 01:33:17,036
(and their first overseas business trip end?)

2439
01:33:17,676 --> 01:33:21,006
(My Genie Secretary)
